[11335]={"Las piedras que Kaleva necesita se pueden encontrar en la bahía de hielo, al este de Sûri-kylä, cerca de la orilla.\
\
Kaleva te ha pedido que consigas algunas rocas para la sauna.","Habla con Kaleva","'Gracias por conseguir las piedras, ${PLAYER}. ¡Has hecho un gran servicio para Sûri-kylä y los Lumi-väki!'","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. ¿Qué te trae a Sûri-kylä? Normalmente los viajeros del sur son disuadidos por el frío clima, pero eso a nosotros no nos importa ya que estamos habituados a ello.\
\
'La sauna es utilizada por nuestra gente para relajarse y refrescarse. Normalmente guardamos un suministro extra de rocas para calentarlas y producir el vapor, pero no hemos podido buscarlas estos últimos días debido a las ventiscas.\
\
'Puedes encontrar rocas por toda la bahía de hielo, al este de Sûri-kylä, cerca de la orilla. ¿Podrías ir a buscar algunas? Llévalas junto al fuego que hay cerca de la cabaña.'","'¿Ya has conseguido las rocas? ¡Debemos tener piedras si queremos construir la sauna!'","Piedras de la bahía conseguidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La sauna de los Lossoth está en Sûri-kylä, al noreste de la bahía de hielo de Forochel.\
\
Kaleva te ha indicado que coloques las piedras de la bahía en montículos cerca del fuego, junto a la sauna Lossoth.","Coloca las piedras de la bahía junto al fuego","Consigue piedras de la bahía (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Piedras para la sauna","'Coloca las piedras junto al fuego, ${PLAYER}.'","'¡Has hecho un gran servicio para Sûri-kylä y los Lumi-väki!'","Kaleva está en Sûri-kylä.\
\
Ahora que has colocado las piedras, deberías hablar con Kaleva.","La sauna es una parte importante de la cultura Lossoth, pero han gastado casi todas las rocas que tenían para calentarlas y no han podido ir a buscar más."},
[11337]={"'Ye are the giant duvodiad Rhus has taken a fancy to? Well, ye don't look too impressive to me. Nevertheless, I'll give ye a chance to prove me wrong.\
\
'Winter is coming on, and it looks to be bad this year. We're running short of meat, and our hunters are too afraid to go for more. Go hunt the white stags of the Gloomglens and bring the meat to me... then we'll talk more.'","'You haven't gathered enough meat yet...what are you afraid of?'","White stags can be found wandering throughout the Gloomglens in Enedwaith.\
\
Caradog Henbuch has asked you to hunt white stags and bring him the meat.","Caradog Henbuch is at Maur Tulhau in the Gloomglens of Enedwaith.\
\
You should bring the meat you collected back to Caradog Henbuch.","Carne de ciervo recolectada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Stoors for the Winter","Talk to Caradog Henbuch at Maur Tulhau","Collect stag-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The white stags of the Gloomglens have a strange taste to them, but we prize their meat nonetheless when winter comes.'","Caradog Henbuch is the village butcher of Maur Tulhau. As winter approaches, he finds himself in greater need of meat for the village's stores.","'Well now... perhaps ye aren't so bad after all! Not many would dare to hunt the white stags... they say the stags are the prey of the Rhi Helvarch, and he wouldn't like his sport interrupted.'"},
[11338]={"Carne de ciervo recolectada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Caradog Henbuch at Maur Tulhau","'Thank ye, ${PLAYER}. We will make good use of these!'","'You've been such a great help!'","'So, Duvodiad -- my apologies, ${PLAYER}...I should no longer call ye stranger. Anyways, Would ye be willing to bring me more stag-meat? Also, Rhosun could use more antlers for her scrimshaw.'","Impressed by your abilities and grateful for the meat you provided him, Caradog Henbuch has become a trusted friend.","Caradog Henbuch is in Maur Tulhau in the Gloomglens fo Enedwaith.\
\
You should bring the meat and antlers you collected to Caradog Henbuch.","Stoors for the Winter -- Repeatable","White stags can be found throughout the Gloomglens.\
\
Caradog Henbuch has asked you to collect more stag-meat for himself and antlers for Rhosun Turio.","Collect stag-antlers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect stag-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected stag-antlers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I'm afraid we'll need more meat and antlers, ${PLAYER}."},
[11340]={"Destruye los suministros de los boticarios (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los boticarios de Urâshi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Boticarios de Urâshi derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Encuentra y derrota a Samûku","Detener la producción","Encuentra y derrota a Samûku en Zikrum-dûl.","Suministros de los boticarios destruidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tu misión es viajar a Zikrum-dûl para derrotar a los boticarios y su líder, así como destruir sus estaciones de trabajo.","Samûku derrotado","'¡Buen trabajo derrotando a los boticarios y deteniendo su producción de venenos! Regresemos a Ub Nishir.'","Boticarios bandidos están convirtiendo el veneno de los usan-kûni. Necesitas destruir sus estaciones de trabajo y derrotar a los boticarios y su líder.","¡Samûku ha llegado para detenerte!"},
[11341]={"Regresa a Hannar","Los Duramano, una antigua familia enana en declive, fueron recientemente expulsados de los Salones de Thorin y de las minas de Othrikar por su traición al Pueblo de Durin, los barbiluengos. El clan rebelde sigue siendo una molestia en los North Downs.","Hay exploradores Duramano dispersos por la zona al norte de Othrikar.\
\
Para reducir la amenaza de que los Duramano se conviertan en algo más que una molestia, Hannar te ha pedido que pongas fin al espionaje sin restricciones de los exploradores Duramano.","Derrota a los exploradores Duramano (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Exploradores Duramano derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Detén a los exploradores","Hannar está en Othrikar.\
\
Deberías regresar con Hannar.","'No me gusta el informe que traes sobre todos los exploradores que se han amontonado alrededor de Othrikar. Los Duramano se están reuniendo en las colinas... eso está claro. ¡Debemos expulsarlos!'","'Desde que echamos a esos malditos Duramano de Othrikar, han estado acechando por la zona. ¡Creemos que están planeando atacarnos y recuperar las minas!\
\
'Tienen varios campamentos grandes por las tierras del norte, y tienen exploradores espiándonos aquí así como llevando mensajes entre los campamentos.\
\
'Pronto estaremos listos para movernos contra los Duramano directamente, pero por ahora necesito que pongas fin a este espionaje. Derrota a tantos exploradores Duramano como puedas encontrar alrededor de Othrikar y las tierras del norte de Nan Amlug.'"},
[11342]={"Defeat Orthadban","'The Golden Host thanks you for your dedicated service.\
\
'Our hope is that, with the defeat of Orthadban, the Black Númenóreans will be unable to summon fell spirits to the ruins of Sâd Doldúr.\
\
'This is a major victory for the Golden Host before we must withdraw from Mirkwood.'","Talk to Faerchiril at Barad Angol","Faerchiril is at Barad Angol, north of Sâd Doldúr.\
\
You should speak with Faerchiril and regale her with stories of your victory.","Orthadban can be found upon the topmost tier of Sâd Doldúr, south of Barad Angol.\
\
Faerchiril has asked you to defeat the foul sorcerer Orthadban.","Defeated Orthadban","On the topmost reaches of the ruins of Sâd Doldúr stands Orthadban, the foul sorcerer that the Malledhrim believe to be responsible for the summoning of fell spirits to the Ashenslades.","'Reports from our scouts indicate that Orthadban, a most foul sorcerer, has made his home among the ruins of Sâd Doldúr. We believe this man to be responsible for summoning the fell spirits of Morgoth to the Ashenslades.\
\
'Will you brave the perils of Sâd Doldúr, seek out this vile sorcerer, and put an end to his fiendish plan?\
\
'Orthadban makes his camp upon the topmost tier of Sâd Doldúr, south of here.'","Stop the Spread","'Find Orthadban and put a stop to his fiendish plans. He makes his camp upon the topmost tier of Sâd Doldúr, south of here.'"},
[11343]={"'Así que encontraste la fuente, jum, juuum. Hoy le has hecho un favor al Bosque Salvaje, ${PLAYERNAME:pequeño amigo[m]|pequeña amiga[f]}.\
\
'Creo que me quedaré aquí un tiempo y vigilaré estos bosques. También me has hecho un gran favor, y ahora estoy dispuesto a colaborar con tu gente de Puente de Caballetes.'","Los ucornos cortezasombría han sido derrotados, pero la oscuridad que los retorció sigue siendo un misterio.","La Encina Malvada puede ser invocada quemando la corteza sombría en la cima de una colina en el suroeste del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Mantoespino te ha pedido que derrotes a la Encina Malvada.","Invoca y derrota a la Encina Malvada","Regresa con Mantoespino","Detener la propagación de ucornos cortezasombría","'Juuum, jum. He hablado con los árboles y vuelvo a estar preocupado. Hablan de raíces envenenadas, aguas putrefactas y un ucorno de corteza plateada llamado, jummm, cómo decirlo en vuestra lengua... Encina Malvada. Toma esta corteza podrida y quémala en la colina cercana. Sospecho que el olor del humo atraerá a la fuente de las sombras envenenadas.\
\
'Ve con cuidado, ${PLAYERNAME:mi pequeño amigo[m]|mi pequeña amiga[f]}, ruuum-tum. Por cómo propaga su violencia a tantos y tan lejos... me temo que la Encina Malvada es un enemigo muy poderoso.'","Encina Malvada derrotada","'Hay que detener a la Encina Malvada para que su oscuridad no se propague por la región.'","Mantoespino está en el sur del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías hablar con Mantoespino."},
[11344]={"Destruye partes de máquinas de asedio (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los orcos Blogmal están construyendo equipo de asedio en su campamento a las afueras de la antaño gran ciuda de Fornost.","Gareth Cope está en el campamento de los Pueblos Libres en las afueras, en el extremo sur de Fornost.\
\
Deberías volver junto a Gareth Cope para informarle de que has destruido un buen número de partes de armas de asedio.","Los orcos Blogmal están construyendo equipo de asedio en su campamento a las afueras de la antaño gran ciudad de Fornost.\
\
Sea cual sea su propósito no puede ser nada bueno. Deberías destruir el equipo de asedio.","'¡Has frustrado los planes de Angmar, ${PLAYER}! Les costará mucho reunir las armas de asedio que necesitan. Al menos durante un tiempo, Puente de Caballetes estará a salvo.'","Deteniendo el asedio","Partes de máquinas de asedio destruidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Informa a Gareth Cope de las armas de asedio que has destruido.","Están montando las partes de armas de asedio en el campamento orco del norte de Fornost.\
\
Deberías destruir las partes de las armas de asedio que los orcos Blogmal están montando."},
[11345]={"Huargos enfermos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Cuidado. Algún idiota ha colocado carne en mal estado aquí.'\
\
Cuando le cuentas el plan a Merruth, su rostro empieza a parecer preocupado.\
\
'La pereza de mi hermano ha llegado a un nuevo límite. Los huargos están enfermos, como preveía. Sin embargo, aunque la enfermedad se haya propagado rápido, no les está matando a la misma velocidad. Las criaturas están propagando la enfermedad a los animales de su alrededor.\
\
'Si te cruzas con algún huargo enfermo, acaba con él. ¡Son un peligro para todos!'","Habla con Maeriel","Parando la propagación","Merruth te ha pedido que hables con su hermana, Maeriel, para ver qué se puede hacer con los huargos enfermos.\
\
Maeriel está en la Pradera de Juncos, en Cardolan.","Acaba con huargos enfermos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deberías decirle a MAeriel que has acabado con muchos huargos enfermos.\
\
Maeriel está en la Pradera de Juncos, en Cardolan.","La hermana de Merruth, Maeriel, te ha dicho que acabes con huargos enfermos antes de que se propague la enfermedad.\
\
Los huargos enfermos pueden encontrarse en la Pradera de Juncos.","'Gracias. Siento que tengas que arreglar el desastre de mi hermano. A lo mejor esto le sirve para pensar antes de actuar.'","¡Merruth ha puesto en marcha su plan con la carne de jabalí, con unos resultados preocupantes!","'Bueno, parece que el plan no ha salido como esperaba. Pero hemos reducido la población de jabalíes. ¡Eso funcionó! Pero, como ves, es posible que haya usado la carne que me diste para envenenar a los huargos.\
\
'La carne envenenda debilitó a los huargos con la enfermedad, como planeé. Pero me he dado cuenta de que los huargos son más fuertes y la enfermedad no está teniendo el efecto que quería.\
\
'Aunque ha frenado un poco a estas criaturas, los huargos no están muriendo como esperaba. Si pudieras ayudarme de nuevo, habla con mi hermana Maeriel. ¡Siempre sabe qué hacer y le encanta mandar! Seguro que tiene un plan. La he visto al otro lado del agua, pero no quiero decirle lo que he hecho. ¡Es muy cruel! Aunque no creo que lo sea contigo. Espero.'"},
[11346]={"Although the Woodmen survived the long siege of Hultvís during the War, many hunters fell to the Orcs of the Misty Mountains.","Madelgard can be found in Hultvís.\
\
You have gathered many cuts of meat from the boars at Málvang and should now deliver them to Madelgard.","Deliver the cuts of boar meat to Madelgard","Collect meat from boars at Málvang (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Would you aid me with another matter, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'When a group of hunters from Blómgard passed through Hultvís, I heard from them that a sounder of wild boars has begun to graze in the ruins of Málvang.\
\
'Hultvís was fortunate enough to endure the Orcs of the mountains, but many of our eldest hunters fell in battle before the War was ended. Those that remain hunt the beasts at the woods' edge, but your aid would be most welcome! If it is not too much trouble, I would ask that you gather meat from the boars at Málvang. Even a small bounty of meat could be of great use to us!\
\
'I know this may seem a trivial task to you, but Hultvís must be prepared if the Orcs return.'","Boars can be found at Málvang in southern Woodsedge.\
\
Madelgard has asked you to hunt boars at Málvang and gather meat for the Woodmen of Hultvís.","'It is no wonder such tales are told of your deeds, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'You've done more than enough to help us. Leave what you have gathered, and I'll see that it gets to the chieftain!'","Collected meat from boars at Málvang (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Stores for Hultvís"},
[11348]={"'Si escucho cosas buenas sobre tu trabajo, tal vez hablemos de lo que podemos hacer por los Montaraces.'","'¿Así que los Montaraces de repente quieren honrar su parte de nuestro antiguo acuerdo? Tiene gracia cómo en cuanto las cosas empiezan a irles mal, buscan ayuda, y sin embargo se la niegan a otros que la han necesitado durante tanto tiempo. Aun así, el hecho de que estés aquí demuestra que se ha dado un pequeño paso. Ya veremos si lo dicen en serio.\
\
'Antes de ocuparnos de lo que quieren, tenemos que asegurarnos de estar bien preparados para el invierno. Las tormentas llegarán pronto, y nuestras reservas de casi todo están muy bajas.\
\
'Si de verdad quieres restaurar este pacto, empecemos por nuestras necesidades. Ve a ver a varios de los habitantes, y ellos te dirán qué necesitamos.'","El invierno en Ost Forod es largo y peligroso. Los vientos invernales soplan con fuerza desde Forochel al norte.","Varios de los habitantes de Ost Forod tienen trabajo que debe hacerse antes de que llegue el invierno.\
\
Basilio Resinas te dijo que antes de hacer lo que los Montaraces quieren, primero deben atenderse varias de las necesidades del pueblo.","Ayuda a Ballard Wilmer","Reservas para el invierno","Basilio Resinas está en Ost Forod.\
\
Basilio Resinas se alegrará de saber que Ost Forod está abastecido y preparado para un largo invierno.","Habla con Basilio Resinas en Ost Forod","Ayuda a Rowena Guardacotos","Ayuda a Clark Cercapiedra","'La gente del pueblo ha hablado bien de ti. Creo que pude haber sido demasiado duro antes... tus intenciones parecen bastante genuinas. Quizás ahora es nuestro momento de dar un paso al frente.'","Ayuda a Poppy Silleras"},
[11349]={"Talk to Thenca atop Helm's Dike","Saruman's Orcs have advanced upon the eastern side of Helm's Dike, and you must stand against them with Cenric, Thenca, and Gamling.","'What can we do? Its iron casing will surely repel any of our weapons, and it will take only minutes to melt through the gate.\
\
'We may not be able to destroy this machine, but we can slow the progress of the Orcs that accompany it!'","Thenca stands atop Helm's Dike, awaiting your attention.","'When the Orcs come through the gate, no man will be long able to stand before them, no matter the strength of his spirit or the depth of his courage. They will pass right by here on their way to the fortress, but some of our bloodthirsty foes will turn their attention upon the horses tied at stable. These good creatures will be helpless!\
\
'Help me untie our proud beasts and set them free! At least that way they may be able to fight back against those who come to destroy us!'","Cuento histórico: Empalizada de Helm","Talk to Cenric by the stable at Helm's Dike","As the soldiers of Rohan fight the invading Orcs on the western side of the Dike, Gamling has called you to him.","Thenca, one of the Rohirrim defenders of Helm's Dike, has asked for your help carrying bolts to the forward ballista.","Talk to Thenca by the stables near Helm's Dike","Freed a noble steed of Rohan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cenric has stopped by the stables, despite the imminent arrival of Saruman's armies.","As you hurry between the defensive encampments at Helm's Dike alongside Gamling and other soldiers of Rohan, you have spotted the great war machine with which Saruman's forces hope to destroy the gate.","'Saruman's supply of Orcs is limitless. We have nothing to gain by remaining here.\
\
'We must retreat!'","Follow Gamling to the far side of the Dike","Thenca is pleased you took the time to free the horses stabled at Helm's Dike, for the Orcs will soon be upon them.","Talk to Cenric at the forward ballista","Follow the soldiers of Rohan to the gate in Helm's Dike","Talk to Gamling on the western side of Helm's Dike","'What good will these bolts do for us? I have never seen so many Orcs before in all my life. These bolts cannot slay more than three or four at a time, and that only if our aim is unfailing!\
\
'My wife and my daughter shelter in the caves behind the Deep, but for how long can we keep the Orcs at bay?'","'It was a good thought to untie the horses, for now they will not be left defenceless in the face of our enemies. Even a cornered animal might slay an Orc or two.'\
\
Thenca looks at you sternly.\
\
'This seems to me clear, ${PLAYER}. We cannot hold the Dike any longer, and the men at Helm's Deep are truly cornered themselves, and we with them. The Orcs will see how ferocious we can be! To the fortress, my friends!'","Saruman's forces march toward the fortress of Helm's Deep. Only one barrier stands in the way of Saruman's armies: the rampart of Helm's Dike, built across the trench through which Saruman's forces must pass. If the gate is broken, the green expanse before the wall will be laid bare to Rohan's approaching foes.","'We need to get to the other side of the Dike, ${PLAYER}!'","Cenric despairs that the steeds of the Rohirrim stabled at Helm's Dike will be slain by the invading Orcs, and he seeks your help untying the proud creatures so they may fight back against the aggressors.","Saruman's Orcs have advanced upon the western side of Helm's Dike, and you must stand against them with Cenric, Thenca, and Gamling.","'What did you say your name was? ${PLAYER}?\
\
'Gamling asked me to bring these bolts to the forward ballista. Will you aid me? Quickly now!'","Talk to Thenca at Helm's Dike","Fight alongside Cenric at Helm's Dike","Fight alongside Thenca at Helm's Dike","Pick up one of the ballista bolts near Thenca","Gamling has called for you at the eastern side of Helm's Dike.","Untie horses stabled at Helm's Dike (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gamling has called for your assistance as he hurries to the far side of the Dike, there to combat Saruman's forces before they can crush the Rohirrim defenders.","Cenric accepted the bolts you and Thenca brought to the forward ballista, but he wears a worried expression, and his face is lined with fear.","Gamling has ordered you and the other soldiers of Rohan to fall back from the defence of Helm's Dike."},
[11350]={"Talk to Egláf by the rock trap on the Deeping Wall","Legolas stands atop the Deeping Wall, ready for battle.","Push ladders away from the wall","Two more rock traps have been loaded atop the Deeping Wall, and Egláf waits for you to release their deadly contents onto the Orcs below.","Orcs have gained access to one of the towers and dealt Egláf a grievous blow. Protect him from their weapons!","Talk to Legolas atop the Deeping Wall","'${PLAYER}, are you all right? My sword has ended the life of many an Orc this night, but even so there seems to be no end to the creatures! Let there be no end to our courage either!'","Drop the readied stones from the west trap","Defeat the Orcs on top of the tower above the Deeping Wall","Talk to Thenca atop the tower above the Deeping Wall","Orcs have climbed onto the top of the tower, and Egláf has sent you to clear them away.","'I will be all right, my friend. The wind was knocked from my lungs and I received a few scrapes, but nothing serious. The Orcs are beginning to overrun our position; I hear them atop the tower!'","Saruman's assault upon the defenders of Helm's Deep has begun, his forces scaling the Deeping Wall seeking to put an end to the people of Rohan.","'Our supply of stones runs low; even were it otherwise, the Orcs would learn to avoid the outlets from which fall the rocks. The cost of that knowledge was high, but the effectiveness of our traps is at an end. For every Orc we slay, five take his place! At this rate we will be overrun.\
\
'Come with me, ${PLAYER}. We are needed elsewhere on the wall!'","Patrol the wall and defeat Orcs as they climb up and attack","There seems to be no end to Saruman's Orcs, but Thenca has sworn to defend the Deeping Wall and will do so with his life, if that proves necessary.","Orcs climb up the ladders leaning against the Deeping Wall and must be defeated. Legolas also asked you to push down as many of the ladders as you can.","The surprise Orc attack knocked Egláf down, but he has recovered from the surprise and wishes to speak to you.","Egláf has called for you to come to his aid.","Drop the readied stones from the remaining traps","Cuento histórico: El Muro del Bajo","Thenca has followed you onto the top of the tower above the Deeping Wall.","Thenca has followed you onto the top of the tower","Defend Thenca and keep him alive","'The battle is joined, ${PLAYER}! Saruman's Orcs felled many trees on the outskirts of Fangorn, and from those trunks they assembled great wooden ladders. They use these to scale the Deeping Wall! Even now the Orcs use these constructions to come within reach of axe and sword!\
\
'My arrows will teach them this is folly, for I can slay many of them before they reach the top; but I cannot bring them all down. You and the other defenders must fight those Orcs who reach the top of the wall. Take the time to push down as many ladders as you can and you will slow their progress, my friend. Now we fight for Rohan.'","Egláf has loaded the western rock trap on the Deeping Wall and waits for you to set it off.","Orcs continue to climb up the ladders leaning against the Deeping Wall and must be defeated. You should continue to knock down their ladders, slowing their progress.","Defend Egláf from the Orcs"},
[11351]={"Talk to Burnoth in the Deeping-coomb","Saruman's foul craft has claimed the lives of both his own Orc-warriors and Rohirrim defenders on the Deeping Wall. Now his forces seek to gain access to the valley through the wreckage that remains.","Aragorn has asked you to defeat the Orcs and Dunlendings that have passed through the hole in the Deeping Wall and threaten the Rohirrim within the Deeping-coomb. He also wants you to extinguish the lit fuses on any black powder devices you find.","Egláf needs your help to retreat further into the Deeping-coomb.","'The victory is ours, and the night is not yet ended; there will be plenty of time for more deeds of valour, my friend. Ah, do not worry yourself on our account! The Riders Four have seen worse scrapes than this, and I deem you have as well.\
\
'Take care of yourself, ${PLAYER}, and of Théoden King! We will defend Rohan to the very last!'","'I should have known to see you here, ${PLAYER}, for heroes such as you are oft encountered where the fighting is thickest and the need most pressing! So it is with the Riders Four!\
\
'Who is this injured man? Egláf, you say? Come with us, my friend, if your leg allows you to stand. You may find a moment's respite within the mill, and take the chance to bind your wounds.\
\
'${PLAYER}! I will bring you to my captain, and to the others. There will be deeds of valour to perform on this night, enough for the Riders Four and more beside, I do not doubt!'","'Saruman has used some foul craft to destroy part of the Deeping Wall, and the coomb lies undefended before his forces! Orcs and Dunlendings alike pour through the hole, wielding sword and axe, but I count other of their weapons more deadly: some of our foes carry devices bedecked with lit fuses. The black powder contained within is harmless on its own, but causes a tremendous explosion when set aflame. Did one of these destroy the wall?\
\
'Slay our foes on this side of the wall, ${PLAYER}, and extinguish the fuses of any lit devices you encounter!'","Cuento histórico: El Valle del Bajo","The Orcs have set more devices containing black powder near the hole in the Deeping Wall, and the fuses have nearly reached the end of their short, dangerous lives!","Extinguish more black powder devices near the hole in the Deeping Wall (${NUMBER}/4)","The black powder within has been rendered harmless","Help Egláf to his feet","You have fought bravely against the forces of Saruman with the Riders Four in the Deeping-coomb, and now their captain Burnoth wishes to speak with you.","Talk to Aragorn in the Deeping-coomb","The Riders Four (and Friend) have achieved their victory!","Aragorn has returned from his sortie with Éomer, and now he has an urgent task for you.","Defeated forces of Saruman (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat forces of Saruman inside the Deeping-coomb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Egláf is injured and needs your help to get away!","Léofdag and the rest of the Riders Four delight to stand alongside you in defence of their land, and together they hope to push back Saruman's forces.","Extinguish lit fuses in the Deeping-coomb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Léofdag in the Deeping-coomb"},
[11352]={"Éomer is waiting to hear of your success in the Glittering Caves.","'I thank you for the kindness of your words, even if they are lies. Yes, I know of the Dunlendings that attempted to sneak into the caves.\
 \
'This is my daughter Léofa. It was she who stood with you and the dwarf against the Dunlending chief, and she has told me all. Do not think to hide such dangers from women of Rohan! We will fight and die for this land, if we must, no less eagerly than any of our men. If you think otherwise, you shame yourself.\
\
'If the enemy finds us here, we will fight to protect the honour of Théoden King and of Rohan. So it has always been, and so it will be.'","Reassured sheltering folk within the Glittering Caves (${CURRENT}/4)","Reassured sheltering folk within the Glittering Caves (4/4)","Talk to Ardith in the Glittering Caves","A woman in the Glittering Caves has heard your reassurances but still has questions for you.","'I hope you are ready for some more fighting, ${PLAYER}. One of Éomer's scouting parties did not come back when he expected, and he went in search of it. It seems to me they may have found the foes for which they searched, and now those enemies might think to ensnare Éomer. Let us go after him!'","Gimli calls for your attention from nearby","Spiders have trapped some of Éomer's scouts and must be slain if the men are to be freed.","Defeat spiders in the Glittering Caves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gimli is in the Glittering Caves, attempting to balance his awe at its beauty with the dangers contained within.","'The folk sheltering in the caves should now be safe from attackers thinking to surprise them from tunnels in the mountains, but there are still foes in the Deep! We are needed outside, my friends!'","Talk to Gimli in the Glittering Caves","Léofa, a child of the Westfold who helped you defeat Lheu Brenin in the Glittering Caves, wishes to speak with you.","Free Éomer's scouts from cocooned imprisonment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Hello again, ${PLAYER}! It is nice to meet in less-dangerous circumstances, even if the reprieve won't last for long! I will fight a hundred Dunlending chiefs, and as many Orcs, if that is what it takes to protect my mother, or my father!\
\
'You came to the caves only recently. Did you hear any news of my father while you were fighting outside? His name is Cenric and he has a distinctive wooden shield, given to him by a great hero before I was born: its edges are trimmed with gold, and it bears an embossed horse's head in the centre. He is very brave.'\
\
You tell Léofa that you fought alongside Cenric at Helm's Dike earlier in the evening, but have not seen him since then.\
\
'Ah, well, I am sure he is still fighting. He is very brave, you know.'","Freed Éomer's scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I spit on the memory of this Dunlending chief, ${PLAYER}. He sought to surprise my people from the rear, breaking into their haven of safety and putting them to the sword under the cover of darkness? He deserves a coward's death, and I am pleased he received it!\
\
'I have sent some scouts to the furthest reaches of the caves in order to find the place where this craven Dunlending entered, that they may collapse it and any others they find. We cannot allow any more enemies to get behind the folk who shelter here.\
\
'While my scouts undertake that mission, I ask you to reassure those who hide here that Théoden's warriors will keep them safe. Will you do that for me, my friend?'","Some of Saruman's allies have discovered tunnels behind Helm's Deep, and threaten the sheltering Rohirrim in the haven they believed safe. Éomer and Gimli need your help to close off these tunnels and prevent such craven attacks.","Éomer has asked you to reassure the folk sheltering within the Glittering Caves that Théoden's warriors will keep them safe.","Defeated spiders in the Glittering Caves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Éomer has come to the Glittering Caves and his anger at Lheu Brenin's attempted attack on his people knows no bounds.","Reassure sheltering folk that they will be safe (${CURRENT}/4)","Reassure sheltering folk that they will be safe (3/4)","Talk to Léofa in the Glittering Caves","You and Gimli have fought a number of enterprising Orcs and found Éomer deep within the Glittering Caves, at the passage where his scouts disappeared.","'I have located my missing scouts, ${PLAYER}, but I was not the first to find them... the spiders found them first! Free my men and let these creatures know that the caves here belong to Rohan and its people!'","Talk to Éomer in the Glittering Caves","Storied Tale: The Glittering Caves"},
[11353]={"Théoden leads a charge of his riders down the causeway into the waiting Orcs, and he has requested that you ride with him.","The fuse on the black powder bomb has been quenched, and the immediate danger has been avoided. Aragorn wishes to speak with you.","Aragorn refuses to give in to despair. He intends to defend the Hornburg even as the Orcs threaten to overrun the fortress.","Talk to Háma","Habla con Aragorn","King Théoden has slain a mighty war-troll, but the beast carried a black powder bomb with a lit fuse!","Quench the fuse on the black powder bomb","Háma, el guardián de la puerta de Théoden, se alza frente a Cuernavilla. Se prepara para recibir noticias de la batalla.","Ride with Théoden down the causeway into the waiting Orcs","Mount your travelling steed and talk to Théoden","Talk to Théoden","'That was quickly-done, ${PLAYER}. You may have purchased us a reprieve, and saved the fortress from another of Saruman's sorcerous devices!\
\
'We are safe, for now.'","Listen to Aragorn and Théoden and decide what can be done","'How fares the battle down below, ${PLAYER}? There has been hard fighting up here, and Théoden King has bloodied his sword already. So far we have turned aside all our foes, but I fear they will storm the lower levels and we will be surrounded. \
\
'Do you have any good tidings for the king, or has all been lost? This night seems never-ending, and that is a trait it shares with the forces of Isengard!'","The defenders have thrown back another of Saruman's assaults, but ten thousand Orcs remain outside the walls. Aragorn and Théoden must decide if anything can be done.","Théoden stands atop the fortress, surveying his seemingly insurmountable foes.","In the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman show no sign of relenting. The defenders have retreated into the Hornburg, uncertain of their ability to long survive against the forces of Isengard.","Storied Tale: The Hornburg","Théoden has asked you to join his riders on their assault from the Hornburg.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Mount your travelling steed and speak to Théoden.</rgb>","'My sword rests no longer in idleness! I am prepared to fight and die for my land and my people! It should have been so earlier, but for the honeyed words of Saruman, poured into my ear by his servant Gríma.\
\
'But no longer! My place is here, in defence of my people until the very end. It will not be much longer.'","'We will ride from the Hornburg and bring death to the Orcs! Riders, to me! Let none fear to ride with us, for the bards will sing of our deeds long after we are gone!\
\
'This is the hour of Rohan!'","'If the Hornburg falls, there will be none left to safe-guard the kingdom of Rohan. We must defend the fortress for as long as we can!\
\
'There is no other choice left to us, ${PLAYER}. It falls to us to save Rohan!'"},
[11355]={"aptura la choza de Gwyllion","Tormenta en Methedras","<rgb=#FF0000>Saeradan ha caído</rgb>","Saeradan espera para hablar contigo en el sendero que asciende por Methedras.","'Confieso que jamás imaginé que la Vieja Mujer de la Montaña tuviera poder suficiente para convocar semejante horda de demonios en su auxilio. Es un alivio que haya sido derrotada.\
\
'Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}, has pasado por tantos peligros.'","Captura la puerta del patio exterior","<rgb=#00FF00>Gwyllion y Echrud han sido derrotados, eliminando así la amenaza de la Vieja Mujer de Rohan</rgb>","Habla con Saeradan.","Captura la puerta del patio interior","Con la puerta al patio exterior bajo tu control, es hora de romper la resistencia enemiga en el patio exterior y abrirte paso hasta la puerta del patio interior y la choza de Gwyllion.","Has acompañado a los Montaraces Saeradan y Amlan para enfrentarte a la bruja Gwyllion, llamada la Vieja Mujer de la Montaña por los habitantes locales de las Tierras Brunas, en su hogar en la cima del Methedras, una gran montaña que domina el valle de Nan Curunír e Isengard.","Habla con Saeradan","El patio ha caído. Ahora solo queda derrotar al líder del asalto y romper el asedio.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Nota: Los místicos del clan del Jabalí contrarrestarán las mejoras que Gwyllion ha puesto sobre sus siervos, pero no combatirán.</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Saeradan debe sobrevivir</rgb>","La puerta hacia el patio interior ha sido asegurada. Ahora puede asaltarse el patio interior y la choza de Gwyllion más allá.","'Temo que esta lucha no haya terminado, ${PLAYER}. Hemos derrotado a Gwyllion aquí, pero ¿quién sabe qué otros aliados puede tener aún Saruman?\
\
'Volvamos a nuestro campamento.'","errota a Gwyllion y Echrud en la entrada de la choza de Gwyllion y reclama el punto de control final","'En las Lomas Ventosas de Enedwaith encontramos por primera vez a la bruja Gwyllion. Allí usaba sus poderes malignos para invocar espíritus funestos en forma de druggavar, cuthraul y cûn annûn para levantar un ejército de antiguos males al servicio de Saruman. Luego, en el Bosque de las Tumbas más abajo, obstaculizamos sus esfuerzos por crear una hueste de espectros.\
\
'Largo tiempo hemos acosado a esta Vieja Mujer de la Montaña, y ahora la tenemos acorralada. Es nuestro deber permanecer aquí e intentar frustrar sus planes. Si logra tener éxito, toda clase de demonios repugnantes acudirán en auxilio de Saruman contra Rohan.\
\
'El clan del Jabalí de las Tierras Brunas comprende que esto no beneficiaría a su pueblo y ha enviado místicos para intentar contrarrestar los hechizos de la Vieja Mujer si intenta volverlos contra nosotros.\
\
'${PLAYER}, avanza y captura la puerta hacia el patio exterior de su morada. Amlan y yo nos quedaremos con los místicos del clan del Jabalí hasta que el lugar esté asegurado. Ve ahora, ¡y que los Valar te protejan!'","Toma el control de la puerta hacia el patio exterior de la morada de Gwyllion."},
[11357]={"Talk to Kyrstig","Defeated hobgoblins in Shakhajât (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It's time to storm Shakhajât! Let's take out as many hobgoblins as we can on the way!'","'Good fighting, ${PLAYER}! We surely dented their numbers. Not bad for a day's work, if I say so myself!'","'How goes the fight, ${PLAYER}? You took down how many? Really? Good work!'","Shakhajât is well-defended by hobgoblins, so there will be no shortage of enemies for you to face inside.","Defeat hobgoblins in Shakhajât (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Storming Shakhajât","Kyrstig will want to hear how many hobgoblins you faced in Shakhajât.","'There's still plenty of work to do in Shakhajât if you're up for it! Get in there and fight those hobgoblins!'","Kyrstig has given you the difficult task of storming the hobgoblin fortress of Shakhajât and facing its defenders."},
[11358]={"Melethon is at the Causeway Forts.\
\
You should speak to Melethon.","'You have done much for the Gondorian army. Victory will surely be ours!'","Defeat enemy guards at Shrak Mauruk (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Melethon","'Orcs and other foul creatures have repurposed one of the old Eastern courtyards into a stronghold they call, Shrak Mauruk. Their numbers are great there. I want to send you in to defeat some of their guards so that we may capture their stronghold.\
\
'I recommend not taking on this mission alone. There are many other able and willing warriors ready to fight. May hope be by your side.'","Storming Shrak Mauruk","Shrak Mauruk is located on the Eastern side of Osgiliath.\
\
You should defeat enemy guards within Shrak Mauruk.","Melethon has ordered you to defeat enemy guards at Shrak Mauruk in hopes of capturing their stronghold.","Defeated enemy guard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11359]={"'See? I knew you could handle it. Didn't doubt you for a moment! The hobgoblins will soon notice that their out-camp has been, well... cleared out... and if we play our runes right, they will blame it on the Orcs!\
\
'They did not know they were dealing with a master of Hammers and Bones, but so they are! And my skill at the runic dice translates onto the battlefield, see if it does not!'","Talk to Klúso near Stazg Vozag","Defeat hobgoblins in Stazg Vozag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hobgoblins working from the out-camp of Stazg Vozag pose a grave danger to the dwarves in the Pit of Stonejaws.","Klúso is scouting near Stazg Vozag.","Defeated Captain Zúrthrug, who did not live up to his whispered legend","Storming Stazg Vozag","Defeated hobgoblins in Stazg Vozag (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The out-camp of Stazg Vozag is slightly north-east of the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws.","Defeat the fearsome Captain Zúrthrug, about whom the whispers gather","'I'm afraid you're going to have to get your hands dirty, ${PLAYER}. To disrupt this camp, you're going to have to fight the hobgoblins and the one in charge here, a wholly unpleasant fellow by the name of Captain Zúrthrug. He's a real bad sort, if half of the things I've heard whispered about him are true.\
\
'But you need not fear any of that. You're a hero, aren't you? This out-camp will be just a footnote in your legend, when all is said and done, and no one will remember Captain Zúrthrug at all!\
\
'Good luck!'"},
[11363]={"'Cuando llegó la mañana, me paré frente al Capitán y presté un juramento para servir a Gondor y al Senescal Denethor, quien ocupaba el lugar de nuestro Rey.'\
\
Logra una sonrisa al recordar ese honor tan lejano.\
\
'Dejé mi vida en tierra con nada mas que mi alforja, la ropa en mi espalda y una espada desgastada de tanto ser afilada.'","'Fue en una pequeña taberna...'","Habla con el polizón y escucha bien su historia. Este es el comienzo de su vida en el mar.","'Es amable de tu parte quedarte. Haré lo mejor posible por ser breve, por necesidad y consideración. Sin embargo, debo comenzar desde el principio para que mi historia tenga sentido.\
\
'Pasé mis primeros años en Lossarnach, junto al Erui. Ese tramo de río conducía al poderoso Anduin y fue allí, en la orilla, donde creció mi amor por el agua. Mi amigo mas querido y yo partimos para buscar una vida como mercaderes, avanzando hacia el sur por el Anduin hacia Pelargir. La vida tiene una forma de torcer tus deseos y pronto nos vimos convertidos en jornaleros y estibadores.\
\
'Fue allí donde conocí al Capitán.'\
\
Mira el agua con anhelo.\
\
'Allí es donde mi vida cambió.'","Habla con el polizón y permítele terminar de relatar los sucesos de aquella noche lejana.","Polizón 01: Un Comienzo Indigno","El hombre comienza a tejer su historia y tú escuchas para que, en sus momentos finales, no esté solo.","Completa la miniaventura: Llamado del Mar"},
[11364]={"'Fue en mi primer viaje, en Pelargir, que conocimos a Yarikh por primera vez.\
\
'Nuestro barco estaba amarrado en el astillero, después de un corto viaje por la Bahía de Belfalas. Mientras cenábamos en los barracones, el barco de los Corsarios se acercó sigilosamente por el río y dejó a sus saqueadores en la parte occidental de la ciudad.\
\
'Pretendían capturar y esclavizar a la población. No esperaban encontrarse con nosotros. Siendo defensores de Gondor, nos lanzamos a la acción.'","Completa la miniaventura: Ataque a Pelargir","Polizón 02: El Primer Viaje","'El puerto en...'","El relato del polizón continúa con detalles de su primer viaje.","El marinero desea hablar contigo para concluir este capítulo.","'En esa batalla contra Yarikh, sabíamos que íbamos a perder.'\
\
Sacude la cabeza, como si aún no pudiera creerlo.\
\
'Aún no estoy seguro de por qué huyeron esa noche. Sin embargo, lo hicieron, y eso impulsó al capitán a recorrer los mares durante los años siguientes.'","El relato del marinero continúa con detalles de un asalto a la ciudad portuaria de Pelargir."},
[11365]={"Polizón 03: La marea cambiante","El relato del marinero continuará mientras rememora el ataque a los Corsarios que encontraron en las orillas de Tolfalas.","Falnavar desea contarte los acontecimientos que ayudaron a trazar el rumbo de su vida.","'Nuestras patrullas en el agua nos llevaron hacia el oeste, a la Bahía de Belfalas. A veces al Gran Mar. Nunca nos aventuramos lo bastante al sur como para amenazar Umbar, pero los Corsarios del sur invadían las aguas gondorianas a menudo.'\
\
Mira más allá de ti, hacia el cielo.\
\
'Una vez avistamos un barco anclado frente a la costa de Tolfalas con las velas recogidas. Lo reconocimos de inmediato como el barco de Yarikh. Nuestro capitán nos dio la orden mientras avanzábamos para interceptar a la tripulación corsaria en la isla...'","'Pensamos que los teníamos; sí, lo creímos. Pero los astutos Corsarios usaron armas que jamás habíamos visto para destrozar la orilla y cubrir su huida en nuestros botes largos.'\
\
Una expresión sombría se extiende por el rostro de Falnavar.\
\
'El Capitán se enfureció y juró llevar al saqueador corsario ante la justicia.'","'Los acorralamos...'","Sabiendo ahora cómo se desarrolló la batalla en la orilla, deberías hablar con el marinero.","Completa la miniaventura: La orilla de Tolfalas"},
[11366]={"Después de oír cómo el capitán y el marinero se volvieron cercanos, es momento de hablar con el marinero una vez mas.","'Era una noche fresca...'","'Nuestro futuro no estaba marcado, pero yo sabía que había ganado el respeto de un hombre a quien respetaba profundamente. Cuando regresamos a navegar, fui nombrado su segundo.'","Polizón 04: Hermandad","Completa la miniaventura: Mi Amigo del Alma","'Nuestro tiempo en tierra, siempre breve, permitía poca aventura. No deseaba aventura en aquellos días; solo camaradería. El Capitán, quien había tomado aprecio por mí solo unos años atrás en una taberna, y yo nos volvimos los amigos mas queridos.....'","Hay mas en la historia de Falnavar y él desea compartirla contigo. Habla con cariño de su pasado.","Aun queda mas en la historia del marinero. Te pide que escuches cómo él y el capitán se volvieron amigos inseparables."},
[11367]={"'Rescatamos a los prisioneros y abatimos al enemigo en la orilla. Pero la tripulación que Yarikh dejó en tierra no era una verdadera fuerza de combate. Eran un señuelo; una trampa tendida por Yarikh. Habíamos caído en la trampa y nuestra nave, Nenglor, y toda su tripulación fue el precio que pagamos por nuestra arrogancia.'","'Fue en una patrulla rutinaria en la punta de Andrast donde nos encontramos nuevamente con Yarikh y su barco, anclado, con un bote de embarcaciones menores a lo largo de la orilla. Había capturado aldeanos en una incursión anterior y debíamos liberar a los prisioneros.\
\
'El Capitán ideó un plan para mantener a nuestros hombres a bordo de nuestra nave y atacar el barco Corsario mientras nosotros avanzábamos hacia la orilla para ocuparnos del capitán y la tripulación.'\
\
Suspira.\
\
'Si tan solo lo hubiéramos sabido...'","Completa la miniaventura: La Nenglor","Conoces el destino de esa noche y el incidente que cayó sobre el capitán y el marinero. Regresa con el marinero para escuchar mas.","Un giro en los acontecimientos de sus vidas; el Capitán y Falnavar se enfrentan a grandes desventajas contra Yarikh y su tripulación.","'Pusimos nuestras lanchas en el mar...'","Polizón 05: El Incidente","Hay algo mas en la historia del marinero mientras su semblante se vuelve sombrío."},
[11368]={"'Nos pusimos a reconstruir...'","'Zarpamos solo unos pocos meses después de estar atados a tierra. Fue entonces cuando lo noté, un cambio en el capitán.'","'Atados a tierra, comenzamos nuestro viaje de regreso hacia Anfalas para informar. Aquellos a quienes rescatamos eran una carga, pero el deber nos obligaba a protegerlos, y así lo hicimos. Las tierras mas salvajes de Anfalas resultaron un desafío, pero llegamos al puerto mas cercano y presentamos nuestro informe a las autoridades.\
\
'Recibimos una reprimenda y fuimos obligados a regresar a Pelargir para ayudar en la construcción de nuestro nuevo barco.'","Con la Nenglor reconstruida, la historia del marinero parece tomar un giro distinto.","Polizón 06: Atados a Tierra","Tras una dura reprimenda por la pérdida de su barco, el capitán se dispuso a construir la Nenglor una vez mas.","Falnavar y el capitán emprenden el regreso a Pelargir después de perder su barco, pero no todo está bien cuando llegan.","Completa la miniaventura: La Nenglor Renacida"},
[11369]={"El capitán parecía estar perdiendo el juicio, de alguna manera. Regresa ahora con el marinero y escucha sus pensamientos.","'Temía por mi amigo. Temía por nuestra tripulación. Mas aún, temía por la seguridad de nuestra tierra si la obsesión del Capitán continuaba. Si aquella tormenta no hubiera estallado y dañado nuestras velas... habríamos iniciado una guerra.'","Escucha la historia que cuenta el marinero; claramente algo salió mal después de que la Nenglor fue reconstruida.","Falnavar reconoce que el cambio en el Capitán es mayor de lo que anticipó, y ahora la tripulación está en peligro.","Polizón 07: Demasiado Lejos","'De vuelta en el mar, zarpamos hacia el sur. Para mi protesta, el Capitán nos llevó mas allá del Sur de Gondor. Cuando cruzamos el Río Harnen, hablamos en privado sobre sus intenciones.....'","Completa la miniaventura: El Sermón","'Estábamos en aguas extrañas...'"},
[11370]={"Polizón 08: Ya no en servicio","Completa la miniaventura: Tramar la venganza","'Partimos hacia...'","'Tras cinco años de servicio a la tierra de Gondor, mi tiempo en el mar llegó a su fin, y también el del Capitán. No fue porque quisiera abandonar el mar. Nos despojaron de nuestra comisión por violar órdenes y quedamos relegados a una vida miserable en tierra.\
\
'Un miembro de la tripulación habló con otras embarcaciones y les informó de nuestra cercana incursión en Umbar. Villanos.'\
\
El hombre inspira con dificultad.\
\
'Después de eso, yo estaba perdido.'\
\
Una sonrisa irónica se dibuja en su rostro.\
\
'Hasta que volví a encontrar al Capitán unos años después. En Pelargir; en una posada. Yo trabajaba allí, en los muelles, y él dijo que había venido buscándome.\
\
'Me contó que había descubierto el paradero del tesoro de un barco Corsario en las colinas cercanas. Me pidió unirme a él para asaltar el escondite y reclamar el tesoro.'","Con ira en su voz, el marinero continúa su relato. Escucha más.","'El Capitán y yo regresamos a Pelargir con suficiente dinero como para retirarnos, cómodamente, donde quisiéramos. Pero algo más grande lo movía a él que el deseo de las monedas. Mientras estábamos en la taberna me confió su nuevo deseo: zarpar tras Yarikh y su tripulación. Llevarlos ante la justicia en nuestros propios términos.'","Falnavar recuerda los acontecimientos después de la casi incursión en las aguas de Umbar y el duro castigo impuesto contra el Capitán.","Ahora comprendes la intención del asalto, y el marinero continuará su historia."},
[11371]={"La historia de Falnavar toma un giro distinto mientras describe la persecución de Yarikh, Hilâma y Akhât, los Corsarios que habían arruinado su noble vida en el mar.","La historia continúa con la persecución del Corsario, aparentemente llegando a su fin.","Una tragedia cayó sobre el marinero, pero el relato se siente extraño; algo en la narración es... inconsistente.","'¡Un nuevo barco!\
\
'La búsqueda de tesoros proporcionó lo suficiente para un barco y una tripulación. Zarpamos de Pelargir y divisamos a Yarikh entrando en Belegaer.\
\
'Lo perseguimos hacia el oeste, hasta que un temporal hizo que ambas naves fueran arrastradas de vuelta hacia nosotros, Andrast y el lugar donde nuestros destinos habían cambiado.'\
\
Un brillo emocionado de asombro ilumina sus ojos.\
\
'Nuestros barcos colisionaron, y nuestra batalla fue feroz. El fuego redujo las naves a cenizas bajo nuestros pies y caímos en el mar implacable, solo para terminar en la orilla cerca del lugar donde habíamos liberado a los prisioneros, pero perdido nuestro primer barco años atrás. Esta vez... fue... diferente...'","'El capitán murió allí, en las orillas de la Bahía de Belfalas.\
\
'El capitán, mi capitán, mi amigo. El agua no lo reclamó como él esperaba.'\
\
Él niega con la cabeza, desolado.\
\
'Fue una hoja del enemigo a quien persiguió durante años, una obsesión que le costó la vida y a mí..... casi me costó la cordura.'","Polizón 09: Ligados a la Venganza","'Los teníamos acorralados y sorprendidos...'","Completa la miniaventura: Marcado"},
[11372]={"'Él... el Capitán me dio obsequios; son valiosos para mí. Los he llevado conmigo en todo momento desde su muerte y ahora, aquí, en la mía... parece que los he perdido. ¿Tienes el corazón para encontrarlos? ¿Para hallar lo que he perdido? Para que pueda tenerlos en mi muerte, donde el agua me ha reclamado y no la hoja de un tirano.'","'La bestia está cerca de aquí. Ve ahora.'","Los relatos de Falnavar cambian otra vez, esta vez hacia los años posteriores a la derrota de la tripulación corsaria que puso fin al Capitán.","Polizón 10: En costas extrañas","Completa la miniaventura: La bestia","La bestia está derrotada, pero se revela un misterio. Regresa con el marinero y cuéntale lo que descubriste.","¿Un desliz de la lengua? No está claro, pero el relato del marinero continúa.","'No puede ser. Lo vi morir con mis propios ojos y ahora...\
\
'Amigo mío, te he fallado. Ya no podemos luchar. Míranos.'"},
[11373]={"Lee la nota que recogiste de Falnavar.","Falnavar ha muerto.","Regresa con el marinero y habla con él para informarle que el cometido está completo.","El estado de Falnavar está deteriorándose y su ultimo deseo es que tomes la venganza que él ya no puede reclamar.","Habla con Falnavar","Falnavar se ha ido.\
\
En su mano sostiene una nota arrugada escrita en el reverso del viejo cartel de reclutamiento.","La muerte de Falnavar es trágica, pero te dejó una nota final.","Polizón 11: Yo, Marinero","To you, who listened to my tale, I give you my haversack; provided that you retrieved it from Yarikh and his crew.\
\
As you likely now know, I am the Captain in my tale. My obsessions led me here - not the call of water. I came to avenge the death of the boy I recruited and befriended and loved as a son. The horror and pain of his loss and the death of my crews is ended.\
\
You have given peace and a final kindness to one who likely did not deserve such.\
\
I go to my final rest with a mind at ease; a desire fulfilled, the scent of salt in my nose, and the sound of the babbling river to send me to my dreams.\
\
Thank you, stranger.\
\
Falnavar","Completa la miniaventura: Una Venganza Final","La ultima solicitud? Quizás. Habla con el marinero para ir al lugar donde está Yarikh y derrota al villano Corsario de una vez por todas.","'Ve ahora y encuentra a Yarikh. Tráeme la alforja que robó.'","'Ve...\
\
'Encuentra a ese perro, Yarikh, y pon un fin definitivo a la miseria que ha causado. Haz que pague por el...'\
\
Tose violentamente, gime y recupera el aliento.\
\
'Haz que pague por el dolor que infligió a mis hermanos... mis tripulaciones... mi gente.\
\
'Cumple este deseo; el ultimo deseo de un hombre moribundo.'"},
[11374]={"Falnavar hizo una pausa, pero parece que tiene más que decir. Pídele que continúe.","Las indicaciones del capitán Aranhir te llevaron a buscar bienes perdidos en su naufragio. Lo que no esperabas encontrar era a un hombre herido a lo largo de las orillas del gran río. El hombre tiene una historia que contar.","'Llámame Falnavar. En mi juventud, hace mucho tiempo, no tenía amor por la tierra ni por el ocio.\
\
'Fui un muchacho duro y brutal que pasaba más tiempo con matones de lo que debía. Minas Tirith, aunque a solo una legua más o menos de mi hogar en Lossarnach, era un lugar de desperdicio a mis ojos.\
\
'El senescal consideraba adecuado mantener su ciudad mientras las tierras exteriores caían en ruina y desesperación. No había escape para un chico como yo que no estuviera en el agua.'\
\
Mira hacia el río cercano.","Habla con Falnavar","'Dejé mi aldea y encontré otra, no muy lejos al sur, donde trabajé bajo el empleo de un herrero, un forjador, un sastre... Estaba buscando mi lugar; ¿entiendes?\
\
'No lo encontré mientras cuidaba los campos, o martillaba hierro. No lo encontré en el estudio cuidadoso, o cosiendo tela. Fue solo cuando miré hacia el cielo, hacia las estrellas y escuché las aguas que mi corazón cantó y se sintió libre.\
\
'Hay una historia de marineros hace mucho tiempo que se establecieron en las tierras de Gondor. Sé poco de la verdad de esas historias, pero sé que nací con un corazón de marinero.\
\
'Y ahí es donde realmente comienza mi historia.'","Habla con el hombre","El anciano está gravemente herido y parece que no hay esperanza de cerrar sus heridas. Su petición es simple: quedarse y escuchar su historia para que no sea olvidado. ¿Lo harás?","Continúa hablando con Falnavar","Falnavar hizo una pausa nuevamente. Quizás deberías ver si hay más que él desea contarte.","'Sí, sí... Lo estoy viendo todo tan claramente ahora. No quiero perderme nada.'\
\
Cierra los ojos un momento y luego habla con voz ronca.\
\
'Alrededor de mi decimoquinto verano decidí que viajaría lejos de Lossarnach. Mis padres protestaron. Querían que permaneciera en nuestra choza labrando la tierra para los magistrados que gobernaban nuestro pueblo desde lejos.\
\
'No me importaban los nobles. ¿Qué me habían ofrecido a mí y a los míos? ¡Pero, la gente! La gente que cultivaba la tierra, fabricaba espadas y mantenía viva la promesa del mañana. Me importaban ellos.\
\
'\\qUn paradoja de creencias,\\q decía mi padre.'","Clandestino: El Viejo en la Orilla","'Perdóname.'\
\
Tose y se aclara la garganta.\
\
'Siempre me atrajo el flujo del agua y el río Erui me proporcionó la única medida de alegría que conocí en mi juventud. Mis amigos y yo construíamos balsas con madera flotante o barriles, y nos lanzábamos por las aguas hacia el poderoso Anduin.\
\
'Era una diversión inofensiva. Hacíamos un viaje, robábamos un paseo en un carro que se dirigía de regreso a Lossarnach, o simplemente robábamos un caballo y lo vendíamos al herrero que lo vendía de nuevo.\
\
'Un sinvergüenza, era yo, con una multitud de otros con ideas afines y deseos: dejar la tierra y navegar por el mar bajo las estrellas.'","'¡Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}!', dice el hombre con una mueca. 'Debería haberlo sabido mejor; y no haber hecho lo que hice.'\
\
Logra esbozar una débil sonrisa a través del dolor.\
\
'Por desgracia, el llamado de las olas y la forma del agua me convirtieron en un tonto, parece, por última vez.'\
\
Tose.\
\
'¿Podrías... concederme un momento para un extraño... para escuchar la historia de su vida... para que alguien pueda saber de mí y así no termine solo como un cadáver arrastrado a la orilla del poderoso Brandivino?'","Sigue escuchando la historia de Falnavar."},
[11375]={"'You return with good news, I hope? Excellent! You have our thanks.'","Stragglers at the Foothill","Return to Tharnion","You should let Tharnion know that you greatly lessened the Orc population at Roz Ladâr.\
\
Tharnion is in Calembel.","A growing Orc presence at Roz Ladâr, near the foothills of the nearby mountains near Calembel promises to become a threat.","'Greetings. I am Tharnion, captain of the guard here at Calembel. I hear that you have offered your assistance to our fair city, and I am inclined to take you up on that.\
\
'Orcs have taken up residence at Roz Ladâr, near the foothills west of the city. Their might was broken during the war, but having so many gather in one place again will only spell trouble. I bid you do what you can to reduce their numbers.'","Derrota orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has derrotado orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tharnion is concerned about the growing number of Orcs who have started to gather west of the city of Calembel.\
\
You should defeat Orcs at Roz Ladâr, their camp in western Lamedon."},
[11376]={"'Halt. If you seek audience with Lord Sirgon, he has other matters to attend. I would ask that you -- '","Stranded Sailors","'I shall talk to ${PLAYER},' Celebros says","Talk to Celebros","Nasar has asked you to bring up the Corsairs' predicament with Lord Sirgon.\
\
Sirgon's manor is located in the north-west corner of East Pelargir.","A guard has gestured for you to stop.\
\
You should talk to him outside Sirgon's East Pelargir manor.","Stuck in a foreign land with no connections, Nasar looks to you for help.","'Hello, ${PLAYER}. I apologize for the cold welcome, but the guards are only doing their best to protect us. My husband is rather busy at the moment, but you may talk to me.'\
\
As you relay the situation to Celebros, she frowns. Her frown only deepens. Even after you have finished speaking, she remains silent a bit longer.\
\
'I must say, this is troubling to hear. Pelargir still bears the scars left behind by the Corsair invasion, and the memory haunts us all. Although, these Corsairs... they are simply men seeking a way home. To be lost for so long, unsure if they'll ever return... I can understand that.\
\
'I shall help them. Not as the Lady of Lebennin, but as myself.'","Talk to the guard in the courtyard","Celebros seems interested in hearing what you have to say.\
\
You should talk to her about Nasar's request outside Sirgon's East Pelargir manor.","A guard gestures for you to stop","Go to Lord Sirgon's manor","'Truth be told, this is a tight spot in which to be stuck. We cannot agree on how to move forward. Othor suggested approaching Lord Sirgon for help, but... even if Othor hails from Gondor, he is a stranger to them. I doubt they would entertain us.'\
\
You mention that Lord Sirgon's family knows of you.\
\
'${PLAYER}, if you're not joking -- and I sincerely hope you're not -- could you tell him about our predicament? Just enough to get him to agree to meeting with us.\
\
'I've heard his manor is located in the north-west corner of East Pelargir, but you must know the city better than I do, eh?'"},
[11377]={"The marooned ship and its crew can be found to the south-west of Aerthir upon the Anduin. A rowing boat on the shore will allow for swifter passage.\
\
Aerin has asked you to help recover pillage from the Corsairs that have become trapped on shoals in the Anduin.","Deliver the pillage to Aerin at Aerthir","Stranded on the Great River","Recover buried pillage near the marooned ship (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Marooned by a foolish captain, Corsairs have stranded themselves and their pillage on a shoal along the Anduin.","Recovered buried pillage near the marooned ship (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'They have taken so much from our people...\
\
'I shall keep what you can recover for us here, for I am sure the Corsairs still had more stored away on that ship of theirs. I hope that when this war is over we will see all of these stolen items returned to their owners.'","Aerin can be found in the lighthouse at Aerthir in southern-central Lebennin.\
\
You have recovered a great deal of pillage from the marooned Corsairs and should now bring it to Aerin.","'The others and I have seen a great Corsair ship marooned on one of the shoals along the Great River.\
\
'Whether they were drunk or simply foolish, the crew is now stranded there with all of their pillage. I would ask that you recover as much as you are able, but leave the Corsairs and let the river claim them!\
\
'There is a small boat on the shore nearby, and it will allow you passage to the shoals. I do not advise swimming, for the current is strong and swift, ${CLASS}.'"},
[11379]={"'The Dunlendings have recently begun wielding weapons that are not of their own make, perhaps in response to the shortage of spears you have inflicted upon them.\
\
'These terrible weapons have edges that are barbed and jagged and inflict terrible wounds upon their victims. Will you enter Brôntrig and try to capture some of these weapons for me to examine?\
\
'Brôntrig lies just to the east of here.'","Recover strange weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Answith reports that the Dunlendings have begun wielding vicious weapons that inflict terrible damage upon their victims.","Recovered strange weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The strange weapons Answith spoke of may be found on the Dunlendings who dwell at Brôntrig.\
\
Answith has asked you to recover the strange weapons from the Dunlendings at Brôntrig.","Bring the strange weapons to Answith in the Isendale","Answith is encamped near the tower west of Brôntrig.\
\
You should bring the weapons you recovered to Answith.","'Do you see, ${PLAYER}? These weapons are of a cruel design. The swords are serrated and the spears barbed... whoever made these delights in maiming their victims.'","Strange Accoutrements"},
[11380]={"Scout Caivád Sâr","'${PLAYER}? I hadn't expected to see you here!\
\
'Did Agnar send you?'\
\
You tell Múta of your efforts in the War of Three Peaks and how you came to be at Caivád Sâr.\
\
'I am glad to hear the war goes well for the Gabil'akkâ. However, if any more of these Dourhands join the fight on Gorgar's behalf, it may not go so well for much longer. The Dourhands have begun taking prisoners, and though they do not seem to be truly allied with Gorgar, they have done much to hinder the Gabil'akkâ. I have also heard talk of a strange dwarf leading these Dourhands, but I know little else of their purpose in Elderslade.\
\
'If you have come to aid me, let us discover the truth of it together!'","Strange Arrivals","Múta can be found somewhere within Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
You have scouted Caivád Sâr and should now find and aid Múta in Tûr Ágal.","As Agnar feared, a mighty force of Dourhands now dwells among the Angmarim at  Caivád Sâr!","Talk to Múta in Tûr Ágal","Múta can be found beside the staircase to the right of the entrance of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
You have aided Múta in assessing the danger posed by the Dourhands and freed Longbeards captured and held at at Caivád Sâr. You should report back to Múta.","Múta kneels in the shadows beside a stairway leading higher into Tûr Ágal","Neither allied with Gorgar the Ruthless nor truly opposing him, the Dourhands and their mysterious leader have rallied to Caivád Sâr where they now dwell amongst the remnants of the Iron Crown.","Múta can be found beside the staircase to the right of the entrance of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
Múta has asked you to aid her in Tûr Ágal.","Aid Múta with 'Disloyal to the Crown'","Caivád Sâr can be found in the northern reaches of Elderslade in the War of Three Peaks.\
\
Agnar Brokentooth has ordered you to aid Múta in assessing and eliminating the danger posed by Dourhands who recently arrived at Caivád Sâr.","'However, there is one more matter to discuss.\
\
'Glóin sent one of his scouts, Múta, to investigate the new arrivals at Caivád Sâr. It is my understanding that you two have met.\
\
'You see, a company of Dourhands has come to Elderslade and it seems they've taken shelter among the Angmarim of the Iron Crown. We do not know their intentions, but their presence here cannot bode well. If we are fortunate, they will not involve themselves in this war, but otherwise, we must be prepared to face yet another force allied with Gorgar and the Orcs of Gundabad. Such an alliance is not beneath the Dourhands, after all!\
\
'If Múta has done well, she will have already infiltrated Tûr Ágal. If something has gone awry, do what you must to bring her back to Zarkul-sulûn.\
\
'Scout Caivád Sâr, ${PLAYER}. Find and aid Múta as best you can!'","'You have been of great help, ${PLAYER}, but our task is not yet finished.\
\
'Whether or not he means to aid Gorgar in the war, Brathar poses a grave threat to the Gabil'akkâ. He must be slain or driven from Elderslade before his Dourhands can cause any more trouble!'","Aid Múta with 'Servants of War'","Find Múta in Tûr Ágal","Múta can be found beside the staircase to the right of the entrance of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
You have found Múta in Tûr Ágal. You should talk to her and learn what is to be done."},
[11381]={"'We must find the purpose of this ash at once!'","Collect strange ash (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sâd-en-Dagor is in Dol Guldur, north-east of Helethir.\
\
Stirnir has asked you to enter Sâd-en-Dagor and recover the strange ash from the Black Númenórean sorcerers there.","The Black Númenórean sorcerers in Dol Guldur use a strange ash in their foul rituals.","Strange Ash","Collected strange ash (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11382]={"Tasgall ha intentado detener la propagación de las bestias de las colinas por todo Fasach-larran, pero las criaturas son demasiado numerosas para que él pueda manejarlo solo.","Bestias de las colinas derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las bestias de las colinas merodean por las pendientes de Nád Nathair, al noroeste del campamento de Tasgall, en Fasach-larran.\
\
Tasgall te ha pedido que derrotes a tantas bestias de las colinas como puedas mientras él piensa en alguna forma de combatirlas más eficazmente.","Derrota a las bestias de las colinas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bestias extrañas","'Vine de Aughaire con la intención de detener la propagación de las bestias de las colinas más allá de Fasach-larran, ${PLAYER}, pero las criaturas son demasiadas.\
\
'Si tienes la dignidad de ganarte la amistad de los Trév Gállorg, me ayudarás con mi misión. Al noroeste de aquí encontrarás un camino que sube por Nád Nathair. Es un lugar peligroso, y de allí vienen las bestias de las colinas que merodean por Fasach-larran.\
\
'Derriba a tantas bestias de las colinas como puedas encontrar allí, y hablaremos de nuevo cuando regreses.'","El campamento de Tasgall se encuentra al norte de Aughaire y al sureste de Nád Nathair.\
\
Has derrotado a un gran número de bestias de las colinas y deberías volver a ver a Tasgall.","'¿Has matado a un gran número de bestias de las colinas? Me alegra oírlo, porque ahora podemos pasar al siguiente paso de nuestra caza.'","'¿Has encontrado a mi hermano? Eso es bueno, pero debes ayudar a Tasgall en su campaña contra las bestias de las colinas si quieres que te recomiende a Crannog.'","'Las pendientes de Nád Nathair se encuentran al noroeste de aquí. Sube por ellas y derrota a tantas bestias de las colinas como puedas, y yo pensaré en alguna forma de combatirlas más eficazmente.'"},
[11383]={"The Rangers of Ithilien had much to contend with before Osgiliath fell to the forces of Mordor, but nothing more curious than a strange group of travellers in Ithilien.","'Being back in Henneth Annûn has stirred my memories, ${PLAYER}...\
\
'Before you and I met in Osgiliath, our company was stationed here and Lord Faramir still held command. Through my years in Ithilien, I have encountered both beauty and terror, but surely nothing stranger than what we found one night. \
\
'We discovered two Halflings and their strange pet-creature! I swear it is true! They spent time amongst our company and spoke much to Lord Faramir in hushed tones... but we came to know them as best we could.\
\
'I have some tales to tell of their time here, but I did not overhear as much as Anborn in our initial encounter with them.\
\
'If you wish to know how we came to find them, you should ask Anborn to tell you the tale.'","'You wish to know of the strange company that passed through Ithilien?\
\
'In truth, I wish I had more to tell. A few among our number spent time with them, but their stay was brief and their purposes were kept secret... except to Lord Faramir.\
\
'I can describe what I beheld during their time here, but you will have to speak with the others if you desire to know more.'","Anborn can be found in Henneth Annûn.\
\
Mablung has asked you to speak to Anborn about the strange travellers that passed through Ithilien before the battle brought them to Osgiliath.","Strange Company","Talk to Anborn in Henneth Annûn"},
[11384]={"'Buenas, ${CLASS}. Estoy aquí debido a informes sobre criaturas extrañas merodeando por estos parajes. Se presume que dichas criaturas se encuentran al sur y al oeste, en las zonas inundadas de este lugar. Me gustaría que confirmaras los rumores y trajeras pruebas suficientes de su existencia.\
\
'Si encuentras algo que respalde mis sospechas, asegúrate de recoger una muestra adecuada de su carne. Tengo una amiga que puede discernir la naturaleza de estas bestias simplemente examinando sus pieles.\
\
'Regresa aquí cuando hayas hecho lo que te pido, y seguiremos a partir de ahí.'","Hasta te ha pedido investigar los informes sobre criaturas extrañas que acechan en las Obras Hidráulicas.","Pruebas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Regresa con Hasta","'¿Encontraste algo?'","'Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}. ¿Puedo echarles un vistazo antes de que los lleves con mi amiga?'","Recoge pruebas de criaturas extrañas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Criaturas Extrañas","Se rumorea que las criaturas sospechosas pueden encontrarse al sur y al oeste del Sótano Putrefacto.\
\
Hasta te ha pedido confirmar los informes de criaturas extrañas en las Aguas de Tratamiento trayendo pruebas suficientes de su existencia."},
[11387]={"The presence of the Ruthless Dead is having a foul influence on the Ruins of Ethillorn.\
\
In particular, you notice some relics appear to be saturated with unnatural power.\
\
It would be safest to destroy them.","Destroy corrupted relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Discover the camp of the Ruins of Ethillorn","Strange items within the ruins of Ethillorn have become possessed of an unseemly power.\
\
Destroy corrupted relics in the Ruins of Ethillorn, south of Linhir.","The Ruins of Ethillorn have become host to the Ruthless Dead.\
\
Reach the Ruins of Ethillorn, south of Linhir.","Strange Relics of Ethillorn","Destroyed corrupted relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The presence of the Ruthless Dead has had a curious effect on the Ruins of Ethillorn.","Hopefully this action will diminish the powers of the Ruthless Dead, but only time will tell.","You have destroyed many relics."},
[11388]={"Strange Sights on the Horizon","The strange spires on the landscape can be found north, south, and south-west of the cross-roads in the south-eastern Whitshaws.\
\
You should scout the southern-most spire of ice in the Whitshaws.","Cyneberg has ridden ahead to Dunfast, which lies westward along the Whitshaws road from Forlaw.\
\
You should meet up with Cyneberg at Dunfast.","The strange spires on the landscape can be found north, south, and south-west of the cross-roads in the south-eastern Whitshaws.\
\
You should scout the northern ice-spire at the lake's edge in the Whitshaws.","This place is clutched in the grips of a particularly violent lingering winter","Search the strange spire to the south-west of the cross-roads","The strange spires on the landscape can be found north, south, and south-west of the cross-roads in the south-eastern Whitshaws.\
\
You should scout the western-most ice-spire in the southern Whitshaws.","'Did you find anything noteworthy? Tell me everything -- but I have news for you as well.\
\
'Dunfast is empty!'","A dead horse lies at this spire; you should examine it","Search the strange spire to the north","'I see signs of Núrzum! He was here... I know it. Do you see the great spires of ice to the north and south?\
\
'Perhaps this mysterious artifact we seek can be found at one of those icy protrusions on the horizon.\
\
'Will you scout them while I ride to Dunfast? I worry for the people of that town.'","The winter weather here is especially cruel, and ice-shards pierce the earth like shining knives","Search the strange spire to the south","Strange spires pierce the flat lands to the north and south of the road, landmarks that Cyneberg declares are entirely new to the plains of the Whitshaws.","Find Cyneberg at Dunfast"},
[11390]={"Regresa a Hasta con las notas de Hethuwen","'He examinado las muestras que me trajiste y he descubierto una sustancia extraña que no había visto antes.'\
\
Hethuwen te entrega una redoma llena de una sustancia verde opaca y viscosa, junto con una nota repleta de información escrita apresuradamente.\
\
'Por favor, ${PLAYER}, lleva esta muestra y mis notas de vuelta con Hasta. En esta carta le pido que te envíe a buscar más de esta sustancia. Deberías tratar de encontrar la fuente para obtener una muestra pura y original que podamos estudiar más a fondo. Tal vez entonces podamos llegar al fondo de este asunto.\
\
'Estoy segura de que Hasta espera noticias con impaciencia en las Obras Hidráulicas. Ve tan rápido como puedas, ${PLAYER}. Temo que esto no sea el asunto trivial que pensé en un principio.'","Hethuwen ha examinado el contenido del paquete que le llevaste y ha descubierto una sustancia inquietante. Te ha pedido que lleves la muestra, junto con sus extensas notas, de vuelta a Hasta en las Obras Hidráulicas.","Hasta se encuentra en la Bodega Putrefacta, en las Obras Hidráulicas, muy al oeste del Refugio Sombrío.\
\
Hethuwen te ha entregado una redoma con la sustancia que descubrió durante su análisis, junto con abundantes notas. Te ha pedido que lleves todo esto a Hasta en las Obras Hidráulicas.","Lleva las notas de Hethuwen a Hasta","'¿Tienes algo para mí?'","'¡Debes darte prisa y llevar la muestra y la carta a Hasta en las Obras Hidráulicas de inmediato!'","Hasta toma la redoma y lee la nota con intensa atención.\
\
'¡Esto es realmente extraño! Hethuwen es una maestra del saber, muy versada en conocimientos. Si esta sustancia es desconocida incluso para ella, como parece ser el caso, estoy preocupado.'","Baba Extraña"},
[11391]={"Gladden gloomwaters can be found along the river Gladden.\
\
You should defeat Gladden gloomwaters.","Defeated many Gladden gloomwaters.","Strange Waters","A strange darkness has come to the Vales of Anduin. Vile gloomwaters move along the river Gladden. These creatures should be defeated if the Vales are to remain safe.","Completado","Gloomwaters move along the river Gladden.","You have defeated many gloomwaters along the river Gladden, making the Vales of Anduin safer.","Defeat Gladden gloomwaters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Gladden gloomwaters (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11394]={"Drakes can be found in Arador's End, north of Tol Ascarnen.\
\
Sergeant-at-Arms Caddafrith has asked you to assist her in crafting a horn to call forces to fight against Angmar's army when they assail Tol Ascarnen. To do this, she asks that you collect sinews from the drakes of Arador's End with which to bind the Horn of Tol Ascarnen. She suggests you take allies.","Deliver the sinew to Sergeant-at-Arms Caddafrith","Collect drake-sinew (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${RACE}, we have a mission of great importance for you to undertake. Provisions are low, as you likely are aware, and the Captain-General has ordered that we craft a horn to call resting troops to service. We shall do this, but we need your help, for we must hold these posts at all cost.\
\
'What I must say next troubles me, but these are desperate times, and we must make due with what we can.\
\
'North of here, in the place called Arador's End, you will find drakes. These creatures have very strong sinew that ties their bones and muscles together. I ask that you collect sinew from these beasts so we can make straps to bind the Horn of Tol Ascarnen. Do not travel alone and be careful not to damage the sinew.'","'We have not time to waste, ${PLAYER}. Make your way north with your allies and collect sinew from the drakes. We must be vigilant for renewed assaults from Angmar's army.'","'You have done well. I will set others to the task of cleaning these straps so that we might yet make the Horn of Tol Ascarnen.'","Strapped for Straps","Battle in the Ettenmoors is uncertain, with forces losing footholds as easily as they gain them. The Free Peoples have taken Tol Ascarnen but now must hold the location. To do this, they will need to strengthen their position as best they can.","Collected drake-sinew (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11395]={"Vino Dulce de Fresa — Introducción","Recoge vino dulce de fresa (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Vino dulce de fresa recogido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Conseguiste ya esas botellas de vino dulce de fresa? Temo la reunión sin ellas.'","Baldwin Colazorro está en la Casa de los Mathoms, en Cavada Grande, en la Comarca.\
\
Baldwin te ha pedido que le lleves cinco botellas de vino dulce de fresa para los cocineros de la Sociedad de los Mathoms.","Lleva el vino dulce de fresa a Baldwin Colazorro","'Esas parecen botellas excelentes. Me aseguraré de probarlas personalmente para verificar que cumplen con los estrictos estándares de la Sociedad de los Mathoms.'","La Sociedad de los Mathoms tiene muy poco vino dulce de fresa en sus reservas y no ha tenido tiempo de preparar más.","'Los miembros de la Sociedad de los Mathoms pensamos mucho mejor con el estómago lleno. La mayoría de nuestras ideas no llegan hasta después de las cenas de la Sociedad de los Mathoms que acompañan cada reunión.\
\
'Hemos tenido problemas para encontrar suficientes fresas para nuestro vino dulce de fresa. Una de las tareas principales de los miembros de la Sociedad era salir cada semana a recoger fresas para preparar suficiente vino, pero con todo el trabajo que tenemos encima, dudo que podamos reunir las necesarias para nuestra próxima reunión.\
\
'Si buscas una tarea, tráenos cinco botellas de vino dulce de fresa. Sería terrible quedarnos sin algo que sorber después de la cena. ¡Dudo mucho que pudiéramos planificar nada sin él!'"},
[11396]={"Langhár can be found at Zarkul-sulûn.\
\
You should talk to Langhár.","The Beornings have kept their word to assist the dwarves in their time of need!","Yrsa Spearwife can be found at Shakal-atrâd.\
\
You should talk to Yrsa Spearwife at Shakal-atrâd.","Langhár and Varthmath can be found at Zarkul-sulûn.\
\
You should assist Langhár and Varthmath.","Gave Beorning-made spears to dwarves at Shakal-atrâd (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Yrsa Spearwife at Shakal-atrâd","Confront the raiding party of the Drekvath River","Word has reached the dwarves of a potential threat approaching the battlefield from the east.","Assist Varthmath at Zarkul-sulûn","Talk to Langhár at Zarkul-sulûn","'Skarding walks his own path. You know this. I never worry, for he is the greatest Beorning warrior. Search for him on the battlefield, as I am sure that is where he went. He may welcome your assistance, though I am certain he does not need it.\
\
'Once you have assisted Skarding, locate Langhár and Varthmath at Zarkul-sulûn. They may have need of your assistance.'","'You should assist those of my kin who are here at Shakal-atrâd with me. They may need assistance in their tasks. Time is never on one's side in battle.'","Strength and Fury","Give Beorning-made spears to dwarves at Shakal-atrâd (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The Drekvath River can be found east of Shakal-atrâd.\
\
You should talk to Yrsa Spearwife by the Drekvath River.","Talk to Yrsa Spearwife on the road","Assist Sighild at Shakal-atrâd","'${CLASS}, I must speak with you of an urgent matter. Scouts have spotted what seems to be a raiding party, heading in our direction from the east! It appears that the enemy seeks to ambush us from behind! I do not know how they were able to get around our lines, but we must confront the raiders immediately! They can not be allowed to cross the River Drekvath.'","There is no raiding party to be found, only Beornings!","Assist Thyra at Shakal-atrâd","Shakal-atrâd can be found in Elderslade.\
\
You should give Beorining-made spears to the dwarves at Shakal-atrâd.","Thyra, Sighild, and Hertha can all be found at Shakal-atrâd.\
\
You should assist the Beornings at Shakal-atrâd.","Assist Hertha at Shakal-atrâd","'Thank you ${PLAYER} for all that you have done to assist our efforts in battle. We will prevail soon enough, this I know!'","'Why, ${PLAYER}, have you come to welcome us to the battle? How very kind of you! We are people of our word. If Grimbeorn declares that the Beornings will assist our allies in their time of need, that is what we will do! We are here to help you win this war. Come, let us not waste another moment!'","'Upon first inspection, the spear seems crude to an untrained eye. Hmm, then you feel the balance and notice the deadly sharp tip. This is fine craftsmanship!'","Assist Langhár at Zarkul-sulûn","Find and aid Skarding Wargsbane","'This is a good enough place to assist as any. Some of my kin have ventured elsewhere but do not fear. I have respect for them all in battle.\
\
'Speaking of battle, These dwarves could use some of my deadly Beorning hunting spears. A perfect throw will slice any Orc in twain! Here, take these spears and distribute them to the dwarves at Shakal-atrâd.'","Skarding Wargsbane can be found somewhere on the battlefield.\
\
You should find and aid Skarding Wargsbane.","The path across the Drekvath River can be found east of Shakal-atrâd.\
\
You should confront the raiding party of the Drekvath River."},
[11397]={"Speak with Agazi near the rockslide to the west","Defeat spiny lizards near the rockslide blocking the path to Ambarûl.","Speak with Agazi near the rockslide on the road to Ambarûl to the west.","'These are flawless! Thank you my friend! Ha-ha!'\
\
Balgiba laughs as he takes the tortoise shells from you.\
\
'We shall pack up here and make haste to Ub Nishir. We are happy to help retake the stronghold, and reclaim this land, our homes, from these Orcs and these monsters from the demon-pit.'","'Ah yes, there you are. We are in need of more people who can fight with us. I know of some groups who reside nearby that we may be able to bring into the cause, especially with your help.\
\
'There is Agazi, who last I saw with her band near the rockslide to the west, on the road to Ambarûl. Then Balgiba, he is camped near the Channel of Bâdizal to the south of Maurûsh.\
\
'I ask that you go and speak with them. Convince them to join our cause to retake the stronghold if you can. Groups here have come to an understanding since Utug-bûr opened and we gained a common foe, so them and their cohorts should know to not attack you on sight, though if they do, you need only tell them I sent you.'","'Ah, and who are you? Someone who has lost their way?\
\
'No, no, you must be the one who has been helping Galâmka, and this fight for Maurûsh! He must be wishing for my help and has sent you, or am I mistaken?'\
\
Balgiba appears cheerful but wary of letting you get too close. He stands ready to attack if needed. You tell him that he is correct, and that you were sent by Galâmka to request his help.\
\
'Ha! I knew it! Well, ${CLASS}, I wish to reclaim Maurûsh as well, so our swords will gladly join with his.\
\
'We are working to harden our armours. Would you help us gather some tortoise shells? Their shells here in Urash Dâr are very sturdy, and I am certain we can find some use for them. Once we have enough, my band and I will joyfully join Galâmka.'","Speak with Balgiba near the Channel of Bâdizal to the south of Maurûsh.","'You are back. Have you spoken with Agazi and Balgiba?'\
\
You tell Galâmka of how you helped them and that they both pledged their swords to his cause.\
\
'My friend, this is good news you bring me. I am glad that you could help them, and that they are so eager to retake our homes. We will need that fire in the battle to come.\
\
'I will await their arrival here and get them sorted. There will be more to do when you can spare the time. For now, I thank you again.'","Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir","Collect tortoise shells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat spiny lizards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated spiny lizards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Thank you for your help, ${CLASS}. I see why Galâmka trusts you so.\
\
'With the lizards gone we will hurry to finish what we must here and then make our way to Maurûsh. Truly, my friend, you have not only helped us this day but helped the people of Urash Dâr have safer passage from this land, and these demons who aim to take it from us.'","Return to Galâmka in Maurûsh and update him on Agazi and Balgiba.","Collected tortoise shells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Agazi has pledged her help in retaking Maurûsh","Speak with Balgiba in the Channel of Bâdizal","Balgiba has asked you to gather tortoise shells for him near the Channel of Bâdizal for the armour he is trying to craft.","Bring the tortoise shells back to Balgiba in the Channel of Bâdizal.","Strength of Many","Balgiba has pledged his help in retaking Maurûsh","'What brings you here, stranger?'\
\
Agazi looks as you with hesitation, her posture appearing ready for a fight as you explain that you were sent by Galâmka in need of help.\
\
'Ah, Galâmka needs help with his conquest of Maurûsh then? He has helped me many times in the past so I will not refuse his call.\
\
'We here are trying to clear what we can of the rockslide to make safe the path Ambarûl. People are trying to flee this land and the path to the south contains many more dangers. Our task would go quicker if it were not for these lizards.\
\
'Might you help and rid us of them? That would let us complete our work and head for Ub Nishir.'","Return to Agazi near the rockslide blocking the path to Ambarûl in the west.","Galâmka has realized that he needs additional help to take back Maurûsh and asked you to go speak with some of his associates and get them to join the fight.","Return to Balgiba with the tortoise shells","Return to Agazi"},
[11398]={"Destruir catapultas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Fuerza de la piedra","Torres de asedio destruidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las máquinas de guerra -- torres de asedio y catapultas -- de los Angmarim están en la parte oriental de Ram Dúath.\
\
Tuokki te ha pedido que ayudes a destruir las torres de asedio y catapultas de los Angmarim.","Los Hijos de la Tierra han estado destruyendo las máquinas de asedio de los Angmarim mientras las transportan por Ram Dúath, pero ahora están demasiado bien custodiadas para que los Hijos de la Tierra puedan alcanzarlas.","'Hemos hecho un gran daño a los malvados, ¿verdad?'","El líder Tuokki está en el campamento Suuri-lehmä en Ram Dúath.\
\
Debes regresar con Tuokki para informarle de tu éxito.","'Es bueno que esas máquinas hayan sido destruidas. ¡No querríamos que los orcos pensaran que tienen la vida fácil!\
\
Sé que luchas contra los orcos y los hombres de Angmar por tus propias razones, pero es bueno que podamos luchar juntos en Ram Dúath.'","'Los Hombres y Orcos de Angmar han estado trayendo grandes máquinas de guerra con ruedas por Ram Dúath. Al principio, a menudo se rompían solas. Los orcos tardaron mucho en aprender a mover estas cosas torpes con seguridad por el paso.\
\
'Pensamos, se están esforzando tanto, quizás podamos ayudarles también. Así que les mostramos la fuerza de la piedra y rompimos muchas nosotros mismos, ya que los malvados parecían quererlas tanto en el sur.\
\
'Ahora, sin embargo, han aprendido de nuevo, y las máquinas de guerra están demasiado bien custodiadas para nosotros. Pero tal vez tú puedas abrirte paso hasta ellas. Deben ser tesoros para estos malvados, cosas que necesitan para hacer la guerra en el sur. Puedes encontrarlas en el paso oriental.'","Destruir torres de asedio (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Destruye las máquinas de guerra y muestra a los orcos la fuerza de la piedra.'","Catapultas destruidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los orcos no encontrarán tan fácil luchar sin sus carros de guerra. Has hecho bien, pequeño ${PLAYER}.'"},
[11399]={"'¡Malas noticias! He oído hablar de este bestial Maestro de la Mano Blanca, y los rumores dicen que es muy fuerte, con un amplio mando. Será un enemigo difícil de enfrentar solo con arco y flechas.\
\
'Pero Frosti Sacudetierra es alguien útil, ¿no es así? Esta efigie será valiosa para lo que viene.'","Tras descubrir indicios de malas artes entre la horda de orcos cercana, Brazofero te ha pedido que busques a Frosti Sacudetierra, un enano sabio versado en muchos saberes, para averiguar más sobre los orcos de la Mano Blanca y su comportamiento.","'Deberías informar a Brazofero de lo que hemos averiguado.'","'¿Sí? ¿Tienes algo para mí?'","'¿Qué tienes ahí? ¡Ah, el pobre enano! Salió a explorar y vigilar... qué final tan terrible. ¡Terrible! Bueno, Brazofero hizo bien en enviarte a mí con las pruebas del asesinato. Tengo talento para resolver este tipo de asuntos.\
\
'Así que estos dientes fueron arrancados y usados como trofeos por líderes orcos que portaban el símbolo de la Mano Blanca. Apuesto a que sé quién está detrás de esto. He oído rumores de un maestro orco brutal cerca de las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo, y su influencia es larga. Comanda a muchos de los orcos de la Mano Blanca de la zona.\
\
'Te haré un pequeño ídolo, una suerte de efigie, con unas runas grabadas. Apostaría que atraerá al orco si lo blandes con esa intención. Ahora deberías regresar con Brazofero.'","Entrega los objetos a Frosti Sacudetierra en la Mansión de Thorin","Regresa con Brazofero en las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo","Fuerza de la tierra","Frosti Sacudetierra está en la Mansión de Thorin, junto a los subastadores al sur del trono.\
\
Deberías llevarle las piezas a Frosti Sacudetierra para que pueda arrojar algo de luz sobre lo que podría estar sucediendo","'Al menos nuestro amigo enano ya no yace hecho pedazos entre esas miserables hordas de orcos. Hemos restaurado algo de su honor robado. Lástima por este pobre compañero y por la desdichada misión que lo llevó a su fin.\
\
'Me pregunto si había algo detrás de este ataque. La brutalidad orca no sorprende jamás en circunstancia alguna, pero tomar trofeos no es algo que hagan los orcos comunes. Me pregunto qué fuerza mueve a esta horda en particular y quién los comanda.\
\
'Lo averiguaremos, ${PLAYER}. Lleva estos restos a mi amigo, Frosti Sacudetierra, en la Mansión de Thorin, cerca de los subastadores al sur del trono. Es muy erudito y disfruta resolviendo enigmas como este.'","Brazofero se encuentra en la Guardia Orca, en las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo de Moria.\
\
Frosti Sacudetierra te ha dado una efigie con runas que podría ayudarte a llamar la atención del espectro orco. Deberías regresar con Brazofero en Moria y él te dirá qué hacer a continuación.","'Deberías mostrarle tus macabros trofeos a Frosti Sacudetierra... quizá sepa más que yo sobre ellos.'"},
[11400]={"Give armour to soldiers (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Angbor","You should talk to Angbor, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.","Strengthening the Numbers","'I tell you, my friend, the Haradrim are a devious foe. Do you know they were planning an assault from the south? By good fortune, my men and I intercepted them on our own northward march. I will not bother you with the details, but needless to say, my men and I stood our ground.\
\
'Ah, so, it seems the smiths have some new armour for our men! Would you be a kind ${CLASS} and deliver it?'","You should bring the armour to the soldiers in and around Aragorn's Pavilion, on the after-battle Pelennor.","Angbor has been tasked with arming the men who will march east and wishes to deliver new armour to the soldiers.","'The gleam of new-forged armour should breathe courage and pride into any soldier's heart. May fear take hold of no man.'"},
[11401]={"Reclama la terraza este","'Tras la derrota del hechicero, podremos dormir tranquilos por la noche sabiendo que estamos a salvo. Gracias por vuestra ayuda.'","Reclama la entrada sur","Reclama el puente oeste","Abre el patio superior","Ataque contra Dannenglor","El corazón de Dannenglor es un gran patio abierto con una puerta al sur, un puente al oeste y una terraza al este. Deberéis controlar los tres para poder avanzar.","<rgb=#00FF00>El patio superior está bajo tu control y las puertas de la cámara del hechicero se han abierto</rgb>","<rgb=#00FF00>El patio inferior es tuyo. El enemigo no lo dejará así voluntariamente</rgb>","Las puertas de Dannenglor han sido selladas. Para infiltraros en las antiguas ruinas, tendréis que entrar por el patio inferior y ascender.","El pequeño patio superior es lo único que te separa del hechicero.","Para tomar Dannenglor para la Hueste Dorada y liberar a sus prisioneros, el hechicero que reside allí debe ser derrotado y su cámara reclamada.","<rgb=#00FF00>El hechicero y la amenaza de Dannenglor han sido derrotados. Audaghaim y la Hueste Dorada están a salvo</rgb>","Reclama el patio inferior","Varios elfos y exploradores han sido hechos prisioneros por un hechicero en las antiguas ruinas élficas de Dannenglor.","Derrota al hechicero y reclama la cámara del hechicero"},
[11405]={"Destruye los estandartes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I want those banners down, ${PLAYER}!'","Estandartes destruidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Garrun in the Isendale","Garrun is at his camp, north of Cuvnerth and the mountain passes.\
\
You should report to Garrun and let him know that the banners have been removed.","Banners can be found at the mouths of the mountain passes, south of Garrun's camp.\
\
Garrun has asked you to destroy the Dunlending banners posted along the mountain passes.","'While this action will only buy us a few moments of extra time, those few moments may be just enough for our forces to prepare.'","'The Dunlendings mustering in Wulf's Cleft have posted banners which guide the warriors coming from other parts of Dunland to their camps, and mark the marching route for forces departing Wulf's Cleft.\
\
'Perhaps if we remove the banners, it will slow their muster and lend our forces time to prepare. The banners can be found along the mountain passes to the south of here.'","The Dunlendings have posted banners throughout the Isendale which mark the marching route for the host gathering in Wulf's Cleft.","Strike the Colours"},
[11406]={"Each time the Orcs of Durshulot attack Aslíf, they erode the Gabil'akkâ's resources.","Orkish weapons can be found around Durshulot to the north-west, on the middle tier.\
\
Rékkur has asked you to destroy these weapons and sabotage the Orcs' periodic skirmishes with the Gabil'akkâ.","Talk to Rékkur in Aslíf","Striking Back","Destroyed Orkish weapons (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Every now and then, the Orcs at Durshulot will mount coordinated attacks against us. These attacks have not been overwhelming or difficult to deal with, but there must be a reason why the Orcs are holding back. I suspect the purpose of these attacks is to tire us out, make us waste our resources before the longer fight ahead.\
\
'But two can play this game. Go north-west on the middle tier to Durshulot and destroy their weapons.'","You have destroyed weapons around Durshulot.\
\
Rékkur in Aslíf will be glad to hear the news.","'The job is done, then? Perhaps we guards can finally get some rest! Thank you -- I'm sure I speak for everyone here when I say that.'","Destroy Orkish weapons (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[11407]={"Winsig is in the mead-hall in Walstow.","'${PLAYER}, you have done me a great many services in your short time here.\
\
'I have one more task to ask of you for now. To the east is the town of Walstow and more importantly, the path to the East Wall from which countless Orcs are spilling into our lands.\
\
'I want you to fight your way to Walstow and ensure that the town still stands. Riders of the enemy patrol the roads and will make every attempt to cut you down on your way. Once you make it to Walstow, speak to the Thane, Winsig. She is young, but she has strength far beyond her years.\
\
'May fortune find you well on your journey. For Rohan!'","Defeat Mordor siege-breakers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat goblin harriers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Striking Eastward","Fastred wants you to travel to the town of Walstow to the east and meet with Winsig, the Thane. He is concerned about the number of Orcs that have been pouring into the Sutcrofts and hopes that the town has held.","'I am Winsig, Thane of Walstow. What business have you here? You bring word from Snowbourn? Well then, what is it?\
\
'So Fastred is concerned by the outpouring of Orcs into our lands? As am I, since they pour onto my doorstep.\
\
'Fastred may be brash, but I respect his leadership. If he has sent you to us, he must trust in your skill as well. Now then, if you wish to see Walstow survive another week, we must move at once.'","Talk to Winsig","Fastred wants you to defeat riders on your journey to Walstow.\
\
Goblin and Orc riders can be found just off the road to the east.","Defeated Mordor siege-breakers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated goblin harriers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11409]={"Striking Shafts","'Listen well, maggot. The War-tyrant wants to lay traps for the enemy and so we shall. We've told the goblins in Grothum that they'll be sending us some fools capable of holding a crossbow and pulling its trigger. First we need to get the goblins bolts they'll use to make the enemy dead.\
\
'There are many trees within this land, and though I'd rather take an axe and cleave them all down, the War-tyrant says that'll take too long and wants us looking for the chaff that has already fallen.\
\
'We need to make many arrows for the goblins, so it is up to us to collect as much of the smaller bits of wood as we can. Search across the Ettenmoors and return the wood to me.'","'Good work maggot. A few more now, and we'll be ready to call in the goblins.'","'You maggot! I gave you an order. Get it done or taste my fist.'","Deliver the kindling to Soldier Glat at Tol Ascarnen","Search the area of Hithlad for the kindling needed to make the arrow shafts. Hithlad and the Grimwood forest are south of Tol Ascarnen.\
\
In an effort to better fortify Tol Ascarnen, the War-tyrant has called to the goblins at Grothum and told his soldiers to craft bolts for the goblins to shoot into the tunnel at the mouth of the keep. It falls to you to collect the wood for the shafts.","Angmar seeks to reinforce Tol Ascarnen, employing the assistance of goblin-archers, who hide behind the walls and launch deadly attacks at the Free Peoples foolish enough to enter the tunnel leading to the inner courtyard."},
[11410]={"Striking Their Supplies","'Ah, ${CLASS}, welcome. We can now make use of the information that was in the report you retrieved from Zukhal.\
\
'Her report has made known where the Orcs are keeping their supplies. If we can sabotage those then we can greatly weaken them.'\
\
Galâmka indicates to locations on the map indicating two locations.\
\
'Zukhal marked these areas, one in the north of Maurûsh, and one to the west. I ask of you to make your way to these locations and do what you can to disrupt their supplies in the stronghold.'","Found the northern Orc supplies","Find the Orc supplies in the northern part of Maurûsh","Find the Orc supplies in the western part of Maurush","'I hear reports again of your success in Maurûsh! You amaze me again, my friend. We are unstoppable with you on our side!\
\
'The Orcs have lost much thanks to you. There is still more that we must do to prepare, so I ask that you rest and return when you are ready.'","Speak to Galamka","Sabotage the Orc supplies you have found in the northern area of Maurûsh.","Found the western Orc supplies","Sabotaged Orc supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find the supplies the Orcs are using in the western area of Maurûsh.","Galâmka has asked you to sabotage the supplies the Orcs are using in Maurûsh.","Sabotage the Orc supplies you have found in the western area of Maurûsh.","Find the supplies the Orcs are using in the northern area of Maurûsh.","Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir and inform him of your success.","Sabotage Orc supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11411]={"The Wintersebb-drakes are found north, in sections near the Hoarwell's source and at the foot of the Misty Mountains.\
\
Angmar's forces at Tol Ascarnen are crafting a great horn to call reinforcements to the fight when the Free Peoples return to assault the area. Kaasak has tasked you with collecting sinew from the Wintersebb-drakes to secure the many horns that will adorn the post.","Building a horn to summon reinforcements at Tol Ascarnen requires that several pieces are collected and assembled for an Orc to watch over and use when the Free Peoples make their assault against the fort.","'We'll need reinforcements against these maggots. For that we need a way of calling more forces to the keep. The War-tyrant wants us to build a great horn to summon our forces to patrol the keep, and we'll do what he wants or feel the crack of his whip. This means that orders trickle down to you, and that means that you do my bidding, whelp.\
\
'Take others and head north into Arador's End. Find the Wintersebb-drakes there and slaughter them for the pieces of their innards that join their bones. Collect them and return them to me.\
\
'Whatever you do maggot, don't destroy the sinew. Ruined sinew is useless.'","Talk to Soldier Kaasak at Tol Ascarnen","'This will do well. I'll see that you are rewarded for your effort. Don't let a success like this go to your head though, whelp. You've a long way to go before the War-tyrant sees you as more than gristle on a tasty slab of rat-folk.'","Stringy Innards","'You've got nothing to offer me. Do you take me for some fresh recruit still carrying the stink of brimstone on his flesh? I've a mind to gut you now, but you've a job to do, and I will see that you do it. Get out there and get me what I need!'"},
[11413]={"Wharf master Annúngil has asked you to replace the damaged ropes and pins on the Rosigil. You should pick up the box of pins and bundles of new rope.\
\
The box of pins and the rope are next to Annúngil, on the docks in the Dol Amroth bay.","Return to Annúngil","An investigation revealed that many of the post pins and bundles of rope on the Rosigil and docks were intentionally damaged. They must be replaced, for if left in their current state they could endanger the crew.","You should let Annúngil know that you have replaced the damaged pins and piles of rope on the Rosigil.\
\
The wharf master is on a dock in the Dol Amroth bay.","Strong Pins and Well-woven Ropes","Replace frayed rope (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Is it done? Excellent. I know not who is behind this, but I am determined to find out!'","Replaced frayed rope (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'While you were busy about the Rosigil, I had one of my men deliver a new box of pins. Take it up, will you, and replace the ones that you found filed down. There is also some rope which you can use to replace the frayed bundles you found.'","Replace stripped pins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pick up the bundle of rope","Pick up the box of pins","You are now armed with fresh pins and tightly woven ropes. You should replace the pins on the Rosigil and the rope on the docks.\
\
The Rosigil is moored in the Dol Amroth bay.","Replaced stripped pins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11414]={"Find Mostun and challenge him to combat","'Let us see what you can teach me about combat, ${PLAYER}. I doubt there is anything in the North that we have not seen in Dunland.'","You have defeated Gaenor in combat","Stronger Competition","Mair has asked you to challenge some of the Falcon-clan's best fighters for the purpose of training.","Mair is by a large rock in the northern half of the village of Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras.\
\
You have defeated both Mostun and Gaenor, and the pair have learned some of your fighting skills.","'Look for Mostun and Gaenor in Tûr Morva and challenge both of them to combat so they may learn some of your fighting skills. I would have you fight Kenned as well, but he has not returned from his hunt yet, so those other two will have to be enough.'","Find Gaenor and challenge her to combat","Mostun and Gaenor are somewhere in the village of Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras.\
\
Mair wants you to challenge two masters of the fighting arts in Tûr Morva, so that they may learn from your fighting skills.","'Thank you for sparring with Mostun and Gaenor, ${PLAYER}. I have heard that they are both a-chatter with excitement about your northern fighting skills. They will refine those arts and perhaps become even more deadly than before.\
\
'You have already become a great help to the Falcon-clan! Let Saruman tremble!'","'What is there that you can show me that I have not already seen? Well, let us find out. Prepare yourself!'","'There may be value in the martial training that you can provide us, ${PLAYER}. I want you to challenge some of our most experienced fighters, masters in the martial arts, so that they may learn from you the skills of the North.\
\
'Look for Mostun, Gaenor, and Kenned in Tûr Morva and fight with each of them. They will learn your skills.'\
\
Mair looks thoughtful for a moment.\
\
'Actually, fight only Mostun and Gaenor. Kenned has not been seen for some days. I think he may be out on a hunt.'","You have defeated Mostun in combat","Talk to Mair in Tûr Morva"},
[11416]={"'Así que el campamento era mayor que lo que Krum pensó al principio. Está bien tener más información sobre él.\
\
Afortunadamente, está lejos del camino principal a Jazârgund y podemos evitarlo en gran parte.'","Krum se encuentra al norte de la Cámara de la Encrucijada, cerca de Ninknakh Faltor.\
\
Líkmund te ha pedido que hables con Krum sobre el campamento de trasgos que ha encontrado y le ayudes como puedas.","Krum ha explorado el campamento","Encuentra a Krum y habla con él","'Uno de mis enanos, Krum, ha descubierto un gran campamento de trasgos en la cámara más al oeste del Camino de Durin, que las criaturas llaman Ninknakh Faltor en su vil lengua. Solo ha explorado los alrededores y me ha pedido ayuda para investigarlo más de cerca.\
\
'No puedo prescindir de más hombres para ello, pero si pudieras ir y aseguarte de que está a salvo te estaría agradecido. Puedes encontrarle cerca de Ninknakh Faltor, al norte de aquí.\
\
'Cuando hayas averiguado más sobre el campamento, vuelve a verme.'","Líkmund está en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, al sur de Ninknakh Faltor.\
\
El campamento de Ninknakh Faltor era grande y estaba bien fortificado, y solo pudiste explorarlo en parte. Deberías informar a Líkmund de lo que has averiguado.","La fortaleza de los trasgos","'¿Líkmund te envía? ¡Tu ayuda es bienvenida!\
\
'El campamento está tras esa esquina. Es grande, pero no estoy seguro cómo de grande es en realidad.\
\
'¡Averigüémoslo!'","Habla con Líkmund en la Cámara de la Encrucijada","Krum, uno de los enanos de Líkmund, ha descubierto a un gran grupo de trasgos en Ninknakh Faltor, en el extremo oeste del Camino de Durin.","'El campamento que Krum ha encontrado es grande... tendremos que mantener un ojo en él, por si los trasgos lanzan un ataque contra nosotros. Sería una batalla campal, sin duda...'"},
[11421]={"Thandor, the Gondorian Captain, can be located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.\
\
You should speak with Thandor.","Freed slaves aboard the Corsair ships (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'During their assault, the Corsairs captured citizens from town and ship to serve aboard their galleys as slaves. Although we were able to halt their advance into Gondor, many remain trapped aboard their vessels.\
\
'We no longer have the proper resources to mount a rescue, so I would ask for you to board the remaining Corsair-occupied ships, and free any prisoners of war that you find.'","Thandor has asked you to board the Corsair ships, and free the remaining slaves.","'Well done, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Although this will leave many displaced refugees within our walls, this means fewer innocents being subjugated by the enemies of Gondor.\
\
'Our next move is to make sure they find their way to some place that's safer. We won't be able to keep them here.'","Struggle for Freedom","Talk to Thandor","Free slaves aboard the Corsair ships (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Corsair ships can be reached using the boat to the south of Thandor.\
\
You should board the Corsair ships and free the captured slaves.","DNT Not Used"},
[11422]={"Los elfos de Echad Mirobel han rastreado a las fuerzas de Isengard en Eregion hasta una antigua escuela.","Escuela de Tham Mírdain encontrada","La Escuela de Tham Mírdain se encuentra en Mirobel, en la región suroeste de Eregion.\
\
Gelriwen de Echad Mirobel te ha pedido que encuentres la entrada a una antigua escuela.","Encuentra la Escuela de Tham Mírdain","'Hemos rastreado a las fuerzas de Isengard y creemos que están saqueando una antigua escuela, buscando desesperadamente cualquier conocimiento relacionado con la creación de los Anillos de Poder. Debemos encontrar esta escuela antes que ellos.'","Discípulo del enemigo","'¡Debes encontrar la Escuela de Tham Mírdain, ${PLAYER}!'"},
[11424]={"'Veo que los velos de lo Desconocido aún permanecen estrechamente ceñidos en torno a nosotros. Espero que tus estudios resulten más fructíferos en tu próximo viaje, pues el tiempo que nos resta es limitado.'","Tus estudios sobre lo Desconocido son de gran interés. Ojalá todos esos enigmas pudieran explorarse en el tiempo que nos queda, pero aun con todo el tiempo del mundo, la tarea permanecería inconclusa. Debemos estar agradecidos por aquello que sí podemos completar. Yo —y todo Rivendel— te agradecemos tus esfuerzos.'","Estudios de lo Desconocido — Introducción","Redacta Estudios de lo Desconocido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cachúnir desea llevar consigo al Oeste toda la historia y el saber de la Tierra Media que pueda cuando los Elfos de Rivendel zarpen hacia el Oeste.","Entrega tus Estudios de lo Desconocido a Cachúnir en Rivendel","Cachúnir está en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Cachúnir te ha pedido que redactes estudios sobre lo Desconocido y se los lleves.","'${PLAYER}, te encuentras entre quienes pueden contarse entre los sabios y eruditos de la Tierra Media, y necesito tu ayuda para registrar los misterios de estas tierras, grandes y pequeños, antes de que llegue el momento en que mis hermanos y yo debamos partir hacia el Oeste.\
\
'Si pudieras redactar algunos estudios sobre lo Desconocido antes de partir, me complacería añadir tu sabiduría a los anales que llevaremos con nosotros a Valinor.\
\
'Ten por seguro que los Elfos de Rivendel verán con buenos ojos que emprendas esta tarea en nuestro nombre.'"},
[11425]={"Las arañas fúngicas se encuentran en el rincón noreste y en el lado este de las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.","Regresa con Knakk","Recolecta muestras del hongo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La parte oriental de las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo está infestada por algún tipo de hongo, y las arañas tienen algo que ver con ello. La propagación se produce a un ritmo alarmante...","Knakk acampa en la pasarela elevada que está en el rincón noreste de las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Knakk se alegrará de examinar las muestras del hongo que has recogido. Tendrá que dejar a un lado el rompecabezas del medallón para analizarlas.","Un análisis del problema","Mata a una araña globsnaga","Las arañas fúngicas están esparciendo esporas producto de sus mutaciones. El hongo que crece en ellas parece haberlas transformado en algo muy diferente. Sería conveniente recoger algunas muestras y llevarlas a Knakk para estudiarlas más a fondo.","'He avanzado con el rompecabezas de este medallón, pero necesito dejarlo a un lado y me vendría bien distraerme un poco.\
\
'Vaya, esta muestra que me trajiste no se parece a nada que haya visto antes. Es un hongo de crecimiento muy agresivo. Te lo juro, probablemente podría crecer dentro o sobre cualquier cosa. Después de ver lo que es capaz de hacer, me preocupa mi salud al manipularla, así que voy a deshacerme de lo que me has traído. Ten cuidado al volver allí y al pasar mucho tiempo cerca de esos hongos...'"},
[11426]={"Puedes encontrar sapos, lagartos y arañas por todas las Obras Hidráulicas de Moria.\
\
Águti quiere saber más sobre la fauna local. Te ha pedido que le traigas muestras de los sapos, lagartos y arañas de las Obras Hidráulicas.","'¡Date prisa y tráeme esas muestras! En cuanto sepamos quién se come a quién, podremos deducir qué criaturas tenemos que eliminar para acabar con ellas en esta zona.'","Habla con Águti en la Bodega Putrefacta","Habla con Águti","Águti se encuentra en el campamento de la Bodega Putrefacta, en las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Águti quiere ver las muestras mientras aún están frescas, ya que espera aprender de ellas.","Muestras de criaturas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El estudio de la fauna local","'Estas muestras son exactamente lo que necesito para desentrañar los misterios de las Obras Hidráulicas. Con ellas, puedo averiguar la jerarquía alimenticia y determinar cuál es la criatura más efectiva para atacar.'","Águti tiene curiosidad por la naturaleza de la fauna de las Obras Hidráulicas y busca a alguien para investigar al respecto.","Recoge muestras de criaturas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Tengo curiosidad por saber más sobre lo que acecha en las profundidades de las Obras Hidráulicas. He identificado tres formas principales de criaturas aquí: sapos, lagartos y arañas, todas ellas cosas viles y repugnantes.\
\
'Quiero saber más sobre ellas, sin embargo, y cómo podríamos frenar su crecimiento. Si me traes algunos ejemplos de las muestras, debería ser capaz de determinar quién se come a quién, y quizás pueda encontrar una manera de enfrentarlas entre sí.\
\
'Puedes encontrar estas criaturas por todas las Obras Hidráulicas. Me gustaría ver a estos bichos distraídos de su apetito por mis parientes.'"},
[11429]={"Campamento de Ekhamâti alcanzado","Los refuerzos llegaron y evitaron tu escape","Haz sonar las alarmas en los campamentos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sabragêsh derrotado","'¡Rápido! Debemos regresar a Iridír antes de que lleguen los refuerzos. Has hecho un buen trabajo aquí.'","Derrota a Sabragêsh","Braseros apagados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Alarmas activadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","¡Sabragêsh bloquea tu escape! ¡Derrota a ella!","Soldados suculentos","Apaga los braseros en los campamentos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","¡Escapa de la cueva antes de que lleguen los refuerzos!","Has atraído a las arañas sobre los soldados. ¡Escapa antes de que lleguen los refuerzos!","¡Sabragêsh está bloqueando tu escape! Derrota a antes de que lleguen los refuerzos.","Tu misión es causar disturbios en una cueva conocida por sus arañas, pero que ahora está ocupada por soldados de Ekhamâti. Apaga los fuegos de los soldados y activa sus alarmas para atraer a las arañas sobre ellos."},
[11430]={"Mundsunu, son of Runald and Cadsterre, waits at the southern entrance to Elthengels.\
\
Like his parents before him, Mundsunu would request a favour of you before leaving his home.","'Thank you for helping us ready our final measures before leaving. Elthengels has been a fine home, but I will feel much safer once we reach the gates of the king's city.\
\
'We will begin our journey west momentarily.'","Not everyone is willing to risk their own life and the lives of their loved ones to save the village of Elthengels. Another family plans to leave for safer lands and requires assistance in their final preparations.","Hereléof can be found at the well in the western section of the village of Elthengels.\
\
Runald would like you to ask Hereléof to watch over his home, once he departs.","'Farewells are such difficult things. I cannot bear to speak with my friends and neighbours for a final time... the sorrow is much too great.\
\
'I wish to give a gift to my dearest friend, Frithnyd. She has always admired my golden necklace, and I wish for her to have it. Would you please tell Frithnyd that I have placed the necklace under the small stone in her yard?\
\
'I hope she understands why I cannot tell her myself... it is simply too difficult.'","Talk to Runald near the south-western gate","Cadsterre can be found with her family at their waggon near the southern gate to Elthengels.\
\
Frithynd has asked you to thank Cadsterre for her kindness and friendship and to wish her good fortune upon her journey.","Return to Runald to finalize the preparations","Hereléof has agreed to watch over Runald's home and its new inhabitants","Runald and his family can be found at the southern gate to the village of Elthengels.\
\
Hereléof has agreed to look after the home until the day that Runald or his kin may come to reclaim it.","You have told Frithnyd of Cadsterre's hidden gift and bid her farewell on Cadsterre's behalf","'Greetings, ${CLASS}. Time is short for my departure. Will you lend me your aid?\
\
'My family has sought to leave Elthengels for quite some time, yet I leave behind a fine home that should not be put to disuse. Would you speak with wise Hereléof in town and inform him that he may use the building as he sees fit until my kin are one day able to return?'","'A message from Runald? I understand. I will see his dwelling put to good use.\
\
'Many refugees have come into Elthengels, their homes and farms being burned and occupied by Orcs and Uruks... I will find some trustworthy folk to inhabit and care for the home until Runald may return. His home will be in good hands.'","'Well done. Hereléof is a good man, and I trust he will find a good caretaker for the house.\
\
'My wife Cadsterre has a favour to ask. Would you please speak with her?'","Talk to Runald near the southern gate of Elthengels","'A fine day to you. Dear Cadsterre sent you? Aye, I knew she was leaving, and I understand her difficulty with saying farewell. My thoughts will be with her on her journey.'\
\
You inform Frithnyd of the hidden gift that has been left to her by Cadsterre.\
\
'I cannot believe that she would leave me such a beloved and beautiful gift! I will be sure to think of her whenever I look upon it. Please, give her my best wishes.'","Return to Cadsterre near the gate","Talk to Frithnyd by the fountain in Elthengels","'A pleasure to meet you, ${PLAYER}. A doll? I fail to understand. You seem rather big to play with dolls....\
\
'Oh, you mean Captain Pindle! That is Mundsúnu's doll! I will take good care of the Captain for him. Tell Mundsúnu to visit when he becomes older, and I will tell him all about my adventures with Captain Pindle.'","'Oh, it makes me feel so much better to hear that Frithnyd enjoyed my gift. It still saddens me to say farewell to my old home and friends, but I can keep them in my mind, and they shall seem less far away.\
\
'We must see to our final preparations here, but my son, Mundsúnu, has asked to speak with you.'","Talk to Hereléof outside his home in Elthengels","Barcyne has agreed to take care of Mundsúnu's toy","Cadsterre can be found with her family at the southern gate of Elthengels.\
\
Cadsterre would care to ask a favour of you as she prepares to leave her home.","Frithynd can be found contemplating at the fountain in Elthengels, outside the tavern.\
\
Cadsterre has asked you to say farewell to Frithynd, as she cannot bear to do so herself, and to inform her of the gift she has left behind.","Runald and his family can be found at their waggon near the southern entrance to Elthengels.\
\
With all of the preparations and favours completed, you should speak to Runald one last time before his departure.","'You have done much for those who will stay and defend Elthengels. Will you offer the same aid to those who wish to flee? Do not misjudge them for their desire to escape. I lost both husband and son when they sought to protect our home, but they knew the risks of their actions. I would not force a similar fate upon those not willing to take such a risk.\
\
'Reeve Athelward has abandoned us. The people of Elthengels are resolved to repel the invaders through their own determination and strength. I ask that you leave us to this task, with a final request before your departure.\
\
'Runald and his family plan to set for Edoras. Runald was once an advisor to my husband and a great benefactor to the people of Elthengels, but the growing danger here has encouraged him to depart to protect his family. Search for him near the southern gate of town, and aid him with his preparations.'","Talk to Barcyne in Elthengels","Barcyne can be found at her home in the south-east part of the village of Elthengels.\
\
Mundsúnu has asked that you bring his doll to his friend Barcyne.","'Hello there! My name is Mundsúnu. Mother and Father tell me that I must say farewell to Elthengels and all my friends. I have never been so sad. I hope that Edoras is as splendid as all the stories that I have heard, but I will miss my friends.\
\
'Mother says there is no room on our waggon for my toys. You should tell Barcyne to take care of my doll, Captain Pindle. Captain Pindle will get very lonely if no one plays with him, and Barcyne will be a good friend!'","Sudden Farewell","Talk to Cadsterre, wife of Runald","Talk with Mundsúnu, son of Runald","Runald and his family can be found with their waggon at the southern entrance to Elthengels.\
\
Thane Mildrith has asked you to assist Runald and his family so that they may finish their final preparations in leaving Elthengels safely."},
[11433]={"¡Las instancias de temporada de verano han llegado! Juega las instancias de temporada de verano durante el Festival de Verano.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Puedes acceder a las instancias de temporada de verano desde el panel Unirse a instancia.</rgb>","Juega las instancias de temporada de verano durante el Festival de Verano.","¡Las instancias de temporada de verano han llegado! Juega las instancias de temporada de verano durante el Festival de Verano.","¡Las instancias de temporada de verano han llegado!"},
[11440]={"Snowreap-goblins inhabit Grothum, a village they established east of the Isendeep Mine in Arador's End.\
\
Ned Claybrick asked you to assail the goblins in their home to deter them from future raids on Hoarhallow.","Return to Ned Claybrick at Hoarhallow","Goblins have been the main foe the Hobbits of Hoarhallow have contended with in all their years. They believe with the aid of the Tall Folk they can score a final victory against the Snowreap-goblins.","Sundering the Snowreap","Ned Claybrick awaits your return at Hoarhallow, south and west of Grothum.\
\
You found the Snowreap-goblins in Grothum and defeated them at their village. You should return to Ned Claybrick with the news.","'Such heroism! We are indebted to you, ${PLAYER}. We will not forget all that you have done for us.\
\
'Please take this. The Tall Folk at Glân Vraig said that Quartermaster Ash there would assist all those that give us aid.'","'We welcome the arrival of our tall friends to Hoarhallow. With them, we hope to end the plight which has faced our people for a great long time.\
\
'In the north, beyond the place where the Hoardale rises sharply by the Tall Folk fortress and bends to the east, at the crest of the hill, you will find Grothum where the goblins dwell. We wish to show them that we are not afraid of their ilk, and truly we are not. There are some of us willing to fight, but they have gone off to protect the wood and help the Tall Folk.\
\
'If you are willing to help us, make your way north-east and defeat the goblins.'","'You will find the golbins in their village, Grothum. It is far to the north and east in Arador's End.'"},
[11443]={"Tawardan has asked you to retrieve lengths of black sails from the sunken ships in the bay of the Harlond.","Return to Tawardan","Sunken Sails","You should bring the waterlogged sail fabric to Tawardan.\
\
Tawardan is in the Harlond.","A toymaker and souvenir crafter asks for assistance fetching a special, sunken, item.","'You did it! I hope you aren't too waterlogged yourself. Now I shall be able to make many sails, which means many boats, which in turn means - many happy customers!'","'Hello, hello! If you have come looking for one of Tawardan's famous toy ships, you are sadly out of luck, my friend. I have only two left, and they have already been purchased.\
\
'Oh, you are not here to shop? More's the pity for you! You could be taking home one of my handmade Corsair ships! The perfect souvenir to help you remember your time in the Harlond! Have you been out to see the sunken ships? King Elessar himself swept into this harbour with an army of the Dead! My toy ships are made with black sails whose cloth was gathered from those very ships!'\
\
He dramatically deflates, sighing heavily.\
\
'Alas, I have run out of fabric. You see, there were a few ships close enough to the dock from which I was able to reach out and tear free large swatches. Now, however, the remaining sails lay sinking into the bay, and I am not a strong swimmer. Say, if you would be willing to swim out and gather more fabric for me, I would be happy to pay you!'","Retrieve waterlogged fabric (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Retrieved waterlogged fabric (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11444]={"Recupera contenedores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los restos del naufragio están esparcidos a lo largo del Baranduin, que discurre hacia el sur desde el Coloso.\
\
Gaelnarthan te ha pedido que nades en el Baranduin y recuperes algunos contenedores de antiguos naufragios.","Contenedores recuperados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gaelnarthan está en el Coloso, al noroeste de las ruinas del faro.\
\
Gaelnarthan querrá ver los contenedores que has recuperado del lecho del río.","Lleva los contenedores a Gaelnarthan","Naufragio sumergido","La página que encontraste indicaba a un naufragio en el río que podría contener algo de valor.","'Después de mucho tiempo y paciencia, he sido capaz de leer lo que decía la página que encontraste. Estaba muy desvaído y en mal estado. Casi la destruyo intentando conseguir las últimas frases.\
\
'Era de cerca del final del reino y detallaba un cargamento de llaves enviado río arriba para los Montaraces acampados aquí. Sabía que se iban, pero querían salvaguardar tanto de sus tesoros como fuera posible. Las cerraduras venían en un barco aparte que arribó a salvo, pero las llaves nunca llegaron. Aun así cambiaron las cerraduras, creyendo que era más seguro que nadie pudiera entrar. Una de las puertas cerrada era la del sótano del faro. Necesitamos entrar urgentemente, ya que un mal lo ha convertido en su guarida.\
\
'Esta página indica la localización del naufragio que debería contener las llaves. Busca bajo el agua y trae los recipientes que puedas encontrar.'","'Los restos del naufragio deberían encontrarse en el fondo del río, frente a Barad Tharsír.'","'Bien, vamos a abrir todo esto y ver si la llave que queremos está dentro.'"},
[11445]={"'¿Viste ese destello bajo las olas? ¿De verdad puede haber algo ahí abajo todavía?\
\
'Parece un jarrón. Me pregunto cómo logró sobrevivir tanto tiempo. Supongo que las ruinas deben haberlo protegido de las olas y las corrientes.\
\
'¡Mira allí! ¡Otro más! Ve a ver si puedes recuperar algunos. Si están sellados, el contenido podría ser una gran bendición.'","Urnas hundidas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Aquí no hay nada más que cerámica vacía y empapada. Esta es la razón por la que debemos retomar la ciudad... ya perdemos suficiente de nuestro pasado bajo las aguas del lago como para dejar que Angmar se lo lleve también.'","Orchalwë querrá echar un vistazo a los jarrones.","Varias urnas antiguas siguen bajo el agua, protegidas de las olas por las ruinas de los edificios inundados.","Urnas hundidas","Lleva las urnas a Orchalwë","Orchalwë vio algunas urnas bajo las olas.","Recoge urnas hundidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11446]={"Supplies For Echad-in-Edhil","Bring the supplies to Amroth in Echad-in-Edhil","'The name is Skirfir, and I keep track of supplies here in Díngarth. It keeps me busy enough.\
\
'King Amroth has sent a list of various items needed at the encampment of Echad-in-Edhil. If you are heading that way, perhaps you could take them with you? And if not, well, I can find someone else, but I will not be happy about it! I know you are going that way, if not today then tomorrow. Look, do me a favour, will you?\
\
'I can show you where to look to find everything that Amroth needs.'","Gather supplies in Díngarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gathered supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The encampment of Echad-in-Edhil is in need of additional supplies.","Supplies can be found in Díngarth.\
\
You should gather supplies.","'Yes, these supplies will be very helpful. Thank you for bringing them to me. The dwarf in charge of sending the supplies has been less than punctual in the past, and it is good to see he stalls no longer.\
\
'I commend your efforts, and his. Good day to you.'","Amroth can be found in Echad-in-Edhil.\
\
You should bring the gathered supplies to Amroth."},
[11447]={"'Encontrarás que los bandidos por los campos del sur de Bree pueden llevar herramientas y bolsas de monedas de nuestros trabajadores, pero la mayoría se dirigió hacia la Vieja Granja Dulcésped, al noreste del campamento de Adso.'","'¡Mira eso, las recuperaste todas! Me aseguraré de que se devuelvan a sus legítimos dueños.\
\
'Debo decir que quizá Adso tiene razón al confiar en ti.'","'Saludos, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Tengo noticias que seguramente te harán ver la gravedad de nuestra situación aquí. Adso es un buen tipo, se esfuerza mucho por mantenernos a salvo —y ha hecho un trabajo admirable con los escasos recursos que le quedan— pero sé que no es suficiente. Estos bandidos se acercan cada vez más y no nos dejarán en paz.\
\
'Ya han robado herramientas y bolsas de monedas a los trabajadores cerca de la Vieja Granja Dulcésped. Aquellos que siguen confiando en Adso... y ahora Adso confía en ti.\
\
'¿Qué opinas de ayudar a Adso a demostrar el valor de sus trabajadores?'","Recolecta herramientas de los trabajadores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Herramientas de los trabajadores recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recolecta bolsas de monedas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Suministros y demandas","Bolsas de monedas recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Devuelve los objetos a Buckley Sheppard","Buckley Sheppard te habló de la actividad de los bandidos en el campamento de Adso y de cómo muchos trabajadores han perdido sus bolsas de monedas o les han robado herramientas desde que esos bribones empezaron a intimidarlos. Algunos trabajadores han huido, pero muchos confían en que los esfuerzos de Adso puedan arreglar las cosas.","Los bandidos con las herramientas y bolsas robadas están en la Vieja Granja Dulcésped, al noreste del campamento de Adso.\
\
Buckley Sheppard te pidió que recuperes las herramientas y bolsas de monedas que los bandidos robaron a los trabajadores del campamento de Adso."},
[11449]={"The supplies for Arhaim can be found at the Beorning watchpost between the Gladden Fields and Duskenvale.\
\
You should collect the supplies for Arhaim before heading into Duskenvale.","Collect the supplies for Arhaim","Garsind, the Chieftain of Arhaim, will accept the supplies.\
\
You should deliver the supplies to Garsind in the village of Arhaim.","Supplies for Arhaim","Deliver the supplies to Garsind","'Supplies from Lúfred? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. We have not received any supplies from the north in some time.\
\
'Please, accept this payment.'","Collected the supplies for Arhaim","Orc activity on the road between the Gladden Fields and Duskenvale has halted trade. The trader Lúfred has asked you to deliver supplies to the village of Arhaim in his stead.","'Greetings, traveller. I am Lúfred, a humble trader. Are you headed to Arhaim? Would you be willing to help me with something?\
\
'I have some supplies for the village, but the Beornings will not let me pass. They tell me that the Orc activity on the road has made it unsafe for regular folk like me. Perhaps they are right, as some of the carriers I sent with supplies never came back....\
\
'If you're headed that way and they let you pass, would you take these supplies to Arhaim for me? They are very isolated down there, and will be eager to receive them.'"},
[11450]={"Recoge la caja de suministros","'La victoria es nuestra en este día, ${PLAYER}: los Dúnedain han tomado el patio de Clorhir. La entrada a los estanques de Glinghant es nuestra.\
\
'¡Sin embargo, es seguro que perderemos esta posición si no podemos suministrarles provisiones! Quiero que le lleves una caja de suministros a Harthadril en Clorhir. Estará agradecida por la entrega. Toma una de las cajas de esta pila y llévasela a Harthadril.\
\
'Vuelve a mí una vez que hayas hecho esto, pero ten cuidado: será mejor que traigas algunos aliados fuertes para que te protejan mientras llevas la caja. Los angmarim intentarán evitar que reabastezcamos Clorhir si pueden.'","'Te lo agradezco, ${PLAYER}. No podemos esperar mantener nuestras posiciones de vanguardia si no podemos mantenerlas abastecidas, y no podemos enfrentarnos a la amenaza de los aguaoscuras que infestan Glinghant si perdemos el control de Clorhir.'","Has entregado con éxito la caja de suministros a Harthadril","El intendente Badhordam está en Echad Garthadir, el campamento de los montaraces en el corazón de Annúminas.\
\
Has entregado una caja de suministros a Harthadril en el campamento de los montaraces en Clorhir, el patio frente a la entrada de los estanques de Glinghant.","Suministros para Clorhir","'Clorhir está en un nivel superior de la ciudad, ${PLAYER}. Toma una caja de esta pila y llévasela a Harthadril.\
\
'Deberías traer algunos aliados fuertes contigo para que te protejan, porque tendrás las manos ocupadas mientras llevas la caja.'","Los montaraces han tomado el patio de Clorhir frente a los estanques de Glinghant.","Harthadril está en el campamento de los montaraces en el patio de Clorhir, frente a la entrada de los estanques de Glinghant, en un nivel superior de la ciudad.\
\
El intendente Badhordam te ha pedido que lleves una caja de suministros a Harthadril en el puesto de avanzada de Clorhir. Te recomendó que llevaras algunos aliados fuertes para que te protejan mientras llevas la caja, pues los angmarim seguramente intentarán interrumpir este intento de reabastecimiento."},
[11451]={"Recoge la caja de suministros","'Los montaraces de aquí solo podrán seguir luchando mientras duren sus suministros.'","'Hacemos todo lo que podemos para mantener abastecido el campamento de Fainneleg, ${PLAYER}. Sus montaraces están en apuros en Echad Garthadir, en el corazón de Annúminas, y me temo que sin suministros frescos no podrán aguantar mucho más.\
\
'¿Puedo pedirte que lleves una caja de suministros a Badhordam, el intendente de Fainneleg en Echad Garthadir? Necesitarás una compañía para que te escolten mientras llevas la caja, pues la lucha dentro de la ciudad puede ser intensa a veces.\
\
'La caja tiene muchas grietas y agujeros en el fondo... ¡no dejes que se moje, o su contenido se arruinará! Espero que los Dúnedain controlen la puerta en el patio de Gwaelband; de no ser así, no sé cómo llevarás la caja hasta Echad Garthadir.'","Badhordam está en Echad Garthadir, el campamento de los montaraces en el corazón de Annúminas.\
\
Cuguminuial te ha pedido que lleves una caja de suministros a Badhordam, el intendente de Echad Garthadir, en Annúminas. Te advirtió que no dejes que la caja se moje y que traigas una compañía que puedan protegerte mientras la llevas. Le preocupa que, a menos que los Dúnedain controlen la puerta en el patio de Gwaelband, es posible que no puedas encontrar una ruta segura a Echad Garthadir.","Suministros para Echad Garthadir","Badhordam está en el campamento de los montaraces de Echad Garthadir, en Annúminas.\
\
Has entregado una caja de suministros desde Tinnudir a Echad Garthadir y ahora deberías hablar con Badhordam, el intendente del campamento.","Has entregado con éxito la caja de suministros a Badhordam","'Gracias por estos suministros, ${PLAYER}. Cuguminuial tiene razón: esto debería permitirnos seguir luchando unos días más.\
\
'A medida que ganemos más posiciones dentro de la ciudad, debemos mantenerlas reabastecidas.'","'Soy Badhordam, el intendente de este campamento.'","'No dejes que la caja se moje, trae una compañía para que te protejan en el camino y reza para que los Dúnedain sigan controlando la puerta de Gwaelband; de no ser así, no creo que seas capaz de encontrar una ruta hacia Echad Garthadir.\
\
'No será fácil, ${PLAYER}, ¡pero estos suministros podrían suponer la diferencia entre la victoria y la derrota para los montaraces bajo el mando de Fainneleg! Badhordam es su intendente, y estará muy agradecido por estos suministros.'","Los montaraces en Annúminas necesitan suministros para continuar su lucha allí."},
[11452]={"Recoge la caja de suministros","'Gracias por tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}. Es de esperar que los suministros que le entregaste a Legrindavor se utilicen para mantener el control de los Dúnedain sobre Tirband por un tiempo más.'","Suministros para Tirband","Los montaraces han tomado el control de Tirband, el patio frente a la gran torre de vigilancia en el nivel superior de la ciudad.","'Trae a algunos aliados fuertes contigo, ${PLAYER}, porque no podrás defenderte de los ataques mientras llevas la caja. Encontrarás a Legrindavor en el patio de Tirband, en el nivel superior de la ciudad, desde donde la gran torre de vigilancia domina el lago Nenuial.\
\
'Vuelve a mí una vez que hayas entregado la caja de suministros a Legrindavor.'","Badhordam está en Echad Garthadir, el campamento de los montaraces en el corazón de Annúminas.\
\
Has entregado una caja de suministros a Legrindavor en el patio de Tirband y ahora deberías regresar al intendente Badhordam.","'Hay esperanza de victoria, ${PLAYER}: los Dúnedain han tomado el patio de Tirband, una plaza en el nivel superior de la ciudad, desde la cual la gran torre de vigilancia domina el lago Nenuial. ¡Este es un duro golpe para los angmarim, y no debemos perderlo!\
\
'Pero debemos mantenerlos abastecidos, o lo perderemos. Quiero que le lleves una caja de suministros a Legrindavor, el montaraz a cargo de mantener nuestro control de Tirband. Coge una caja de esta pila y llévasela a Legrindavor.\
\
'Deberías traer aliados contigo, pues serás incapaz de defenderte de los ataques de los angmarim mientras llevas la caja de suministros. Vuelve a mí una vez que hayas entregado la caja a Legrindavor.'","Legrindavor está en Tirband, el patio en el nivel superior de la ciudad, desde el cual la gran torre de vigilancia domina el lago Nenuial.\
\
El intendente Badhordam te ha pedido que lleves una caja de suministros a Legrindavor en el patio de Tirband, en el nivel superior de la ciudad.","Has entregado con éxito la caja de suministros a Legrindavor"},
[11453]={"Consigue madera cortada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Minda te está esperando en el Embarcadero de los Comerciantes.\
\
Deberías hablar con Minda Matosos.","Consigue herramientas de carpintero","Habla con Minda Matosos","Suministros para el carro de suministros","'¡${RACE}! ¡No se podría pedir a nadie mejor!\
\
'Me has ayudado mucho, pero, si te parece bien, tengo una última petición. Las cajas de suministros que me has ayudado a reunir pesan mucho. Sin embargo, mi carro sigue destrozado. Los comerciantes de aquí me han dicho que podemos encontrar los materiales necesarios para construir un nuevo carro en la cercana ciudad de Cotfast.\
\
'Iría yo, pero, ay, está llena de gente malvada, y ya sabemos cómo me iría. Por favor, ve a Cotfast y recoge clavos, herramientas de carpintero, ruedas y madera cortada. ¡Te esperaré en el Embarcadero de los Comerciantes!'","Consigue sacos de clavos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sacos de clavos conseguidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cotfast se encuentra en el centro del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Minda Matosos te ha pedido que vayas a Cotfast a buscar materiales para reparar su carro.","Ruedas de carro conseguidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Herramientas de carpintero conseguidas","Consigue ruedas de carro (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Minda Matosos está lista para partir hacia Bree, pero tiene una última petición antes de poder emprender el viaje de vuelta a casa.","'¡Lo has conseguido, ${PLAYER}! ¡No solo has conseguido que siga teniendo trabajo, sino también todos los ingredientes necesarios para el banquete! ¡Este será un gran día de celebración! ¡Un rayo de esperanza en estos tiempos oscuros!\
\
'Los miembros de la Liga que están aquí se han ofrecido a ayudarme a montar una nueva carreta. En poco tiempo estaré de camino a casa. ¡Gracias, mil veces gracias!'","Madera cortada conseguida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11454]={"Assist in gathering supplies for the army","Feeding, outfitting, and arming an entire army takes vast resources.","Return to Valdi","Supplies for the War Effort","'So, you have come to assist the war effort? We certainly could use the help, and everyone is expected to pitch in. There are numerous tasks that need doing. Assist the others where you can, and lighten the burden where you may.'","'You have done much to help the cause. Our victory will be in part due to your efforts.'","Valdi can be found in Amdân.\
\
You should return to Valdi.","Goods and supplies can be found across Azanulbizar.\
\
Valdi has tasked you with gathering meat, furs, and supplies for the army."},
[11456]={"'I see you have made it out of the crypts in one piece. And there were more supplies inside, as I suspected! It gladdens me that I did not send you into that horrid place for no reason! I will begin taking inventory of what you have gotten for us immediately.\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'","Abandoned supplies collected (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the supplies to Andûmu","The Jatsakóri of Gadim-ûn are running low on the basic necessities they need to continue living in An Shêru.","Wights defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Wights inside the Crypts of Gadim-ûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Andûmu believes there may be more supply caches hidden many years ago inside the Crypts of Gadim-ûn by Ordâkhai soldiers. You have gone there at his request and collected supplies, as well as defeating some of the wights. You should return to Andûmu inside the hall at Gadim-ûn.","Supplies in the Hallows","'Hashtal-gûr.'\
\
The man bows to you politely.\
\
'Is it true that you have come to help us? My name is Andûmu and Nabatínu has put me in charge of our supplies. One of the reasons we are here in Gadim-ûn is that there was a long-forgotten Ordâkhai supply cache left in this place, which we have been able to live off of for a time. Unfortunately, we are quickly running out of these supplies.\
\
'I have a suspicion that there are more supply crates hidden away inside the crypts, but I am unfit for that sort of... adventure. I am sure you have noticed that the Dead in An Shêru are not at rest and pose a great danger to us.\
\
'You, however, seem to be able to handle them. If you would go into the crypts and search for more supplies, it would surely increase our chances of survival.'","Collect abandoned supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Andûmu believes there may be more supply caches hidden many years ago inside the Crypts of Gadim-ûn by Ordâkhai soldiers. He has asked you to enter the crypts and search for them. You should also defeat some of the wights while you are there. The entrance to the Crypts of Gadim-ûn is at the north-west end of the hall at Gadim-ûn."},
[11457]={"Return to Tálbiral in Laivárth","'${CLASS}, I am in need of some supplies from outside of the grove.\
\
'There are flowers and berries that can be found nearby. Bring me some of them so I can check on how they are withstanding the blight.\
\
'I also ask that you look for my notebook while you are in the swamp. I fear I left it there some time ago... and have use of it again. The pages may have been scattered over time.'","'Ah, you have returned. Did you manage to gather what I asked?'\
\
You give Tálbiral the gathered flowers, berries, and missing pages from his notebook.\
\
'This is worse than I thought. The rot has consumed these plants entirely. Thank you for gathering the missing pages from my notes. These will be of great use as I look into how this blight has become more aggressive.\
\
'Please, take this for your troubles.'","Supplies in the Swamp","Bring the gathered flowers, berries, and missing notebook pages back to Tálbiral in Laivárth.","Rotting berries gathered (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find missing pages","Gather rotting flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tálbiral needs help gathering flowers and berries near Laivárth so that he can check how the blight is affecting them as well as recovering the missing pages of his notebook.","Found missing pages","Gather rotting berries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Rotting flowers gathered (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11458]={"'Lleva esa carne de jabalí y esas pieles a Sirvellon en Sírlond con mis saludos, y dile también que mantengo mi vigilancia sobre los trasgos Blogmal que merodean en las Quebradas del Sur. Sírlond está al este de Caranost propiamente dicho, al suroeste de aquí.'","Lleva la carne de jabalí y las pieles de lince a Sirvellon en Sírlond","Haerandir está fuera de Haudh Nirui, en las Quebradas del Sur.","'Mi hermana Maedhril se casó con un Elfo de Imladris. Su nombre es Sirvellon, y lideró una expedición hacia el sur; incluso ahora los dos han establecido un campamento cerca de la ciudad abandonada de Caranost. Su campamento se llama Sírlond.\
\
'El suyo es un amor joven, solo setecientos años según mi cuenta, y a veces creo que están ciegos a los defectos del otro. Sirvellon es un buen Elfo, pero es más corto de vista que mi hermana, y temo que esté tan enfocado en los orcos que no obtendrá suficientes provisiones para mantener el campamento funcionando.\
\
'¿Quizás me ayudes a obtener carne de jabalí y pieles de lince de las bestias aquí en las Quebradas del Sur? Entonces podemos enviárselas a Sirvellon y Maedhril, y me preocuparé menos por ellos.'","Sirvellon está en Sírlond, al este de Caranost propiamente dicho.","Los jabalíes y linces de las Quebradas del Sur pueden proporcionar los suministros que Haerandir solicitó.","Pieles de lince recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva la carne de jabalí y las pieles de lince a Haerandir fuera de Haudh Nirui","Recolecta carne de los jabalíes de las Quebradas del Sur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Sí, estos servirán perfectamente! Esta carne y estas pieles ayudarán a Sirvellon y Maedhril a reabastecer las provisiones que estoy seguro no lograron preparar.\
\
'Llévaselos a Sirvellon en Sírlond con mis saludos, y dile también que mantengo mi vigilancia sobre los trasgos Blogmal que merodean en las Quebradas del Sur. Sírlond está al este de Caranost propiamente dicho, al suroeste de aquí.'","Suministros en las Quebradas del Sur","Recolecta pieles de los linces de las Quebradas del Sur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Haerandir quiere que le ayudes a recolectar los suministros necesarios para reabastecer el campamento de su hermana y su esposo.","Carne de jabalí recolectada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Estos suministros son de Haerandir? Son bienvenidos... pero con reservas.\
\
'El hermano de mi esposa siempre está haciendo esto. \\qSirvellon, creo que deberías hacer esto,\\q dice, y \\qSirvellon, ¿por qué no pensaste en esto?\\q Si hubiera conocido las costumbres de su hermano cuando me enamoré de mi Maedhril... pero no, no cambiaría nada. Ella tiene todo mi amor, y siempre lo tendrá.\
\
'Fue idea de ella enviarlo a explorar en busca de trasgos cuando los tres vinimos al sur, y fue muy sabio. ¡Confía en Haerandir para molestarme, incluso desde lejos! Pero los suministros son bienvenidos. Tiene razón en este punto: nuestras provisiones están comenzando a agotarse.'\
\
Sirvellon suspira.\
\
'Y esa es la peor molestia de todas, ¿no es así? ¡Que el hermano de mi esposa tenía razón una vez más!\
\
'¿Estás casado, ${PLAYER}? Si no lo estás, presta atención a mi consejo: ¡descubre si tu futuro cónyuge tiene hermanos... y hazlo con antelación!'","'¿Quizás me ayudes a obtener carne de jabalí y pieles de lince de las bestias aquí en las Quebradas del Sur? Entonces podemos enviárselas a Sirvellon y Maedhril, y me preocuparé menos por ellos.'"},
[11459]={"Deliver supplies to the resting Ranger","Deliver supplies to the nervous Ranger","Deliver supplies to the tracking Ranger","'${PLAYER}, while you are out there with Legolas, keep watch for my fellow Rangers. Five of our company are already afield and would appreciate some fresh supplies.'","Rangers of Ithilien can be found in the western cliffs of Cirith Ungol.\
\
You should deliver supplies to any Rangers you find. Mírthel said there were five.","'It is done? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I am sure they were pleased to see a friendly face in this harsh land, especially one bearing fresh rations!'","'Ugh. The foul stench from the river below carries all the way up here. I shall have to return to camp soon, before I am seriously ill from the fumes! Thanks to your supplies, I should be able to make it back on my own.'","Deliver supplies to the famished Ranger","Deliver supplies to the ill Ranger","Talk to Mírthel","Mírthel has asked you to deliver supplies to Rangers in the field in Cirith Ungol.","The crate of Ranger supplies can be found in Echad Taerdim.\
\
You should collect the supplies to take to the Rangers in Cirith Ungol.","Mírthel can be found in  Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.\
\
You should talk to Mírthel.","Collect the Ranger supplies","'Oh, ${PLAYER}! You startled me. This area is crawling with gredbyg, and it has me a bit on edge. Thank you for the supplies, but I may return soon for the sake of my own sanity.'","'Thank you, friend. I was growing quite famished, and have not been able to find anything edible in these wilds. The plants and animals are all tainted!'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I have been attempting to follow these tracks, but it is very difficult. The others joke that the men leaving them must have sprouted wings and flew, but that cannot be, can it?'","Collected the Ranger supplies","Supply Run","'I was expecting Mírthel to come with supplies, not you, ${PLAYER}! Thank you for your efforts, friend!'"},
[11462]={"'${PLAYER}, what brings you to me?'\
\
You ask Halshûm if he has any interest in a trade agreement with a Temámir jeweller from Jiret-menêsh.\
\
'Interesting... I myself am not, but I know many people and may still be able to help you. I would need you to do something for me first, of course.\
\
'I sell supplies to the Ordâkhai at Kôth Rau. It is why they allow us to keep Khanâg Gur in business. Among those supplies are foodstuffs that resist spoilage - very useful for an army. I happen to find myself with more of these rations than the Ordâkhai wanted to buy, and I need to sell them. There is gold invested in them, and I need it back.\
\
'Should you find yourself in Kôth Rau, and the rations they bought from me happened to go missing, they would need to replace their lost supplies. Do you follow me? If this thing happens, I will see to it that this jeweller of yours has a buyer.'","'${PLAYER}, you were gone so long, I thought you had forgotten me, but you went all the way to Zajâna on my behalf? I do not know that I am worthy of such effort, but thank you! I have many rings and pendants ready to trade, but I look forward to talking to this Zarzûmir about what is best for selling, and make more of that!\
\
'This brings me so much joy, ${PLAYER}! I cannot wait to get back to my workbench!'","Talk to Halshûm at Khanâg Gur","Supplying Demand","Talk to Zarzûmir in Zajâna","'Most of us who came to the surface did so because we want to trade. Not many visitors have come to us, and there have been no trade caravans yet. Some of the bravest among us have left to make deals with the Temámir of the Shoreward Stone, but I am a jeweller, not a trader, and I am certainly no adventurer!\
\
'I fear that I will be left behind without a trade partner, but I have an idea. I have heard that Khanâg Gur still does business, does it not? If someone were to go there and speak to their leader, perhaps they could sell my goods or take them to a market elsewhere?'\
\
You warn her that the leader of Khanâg Gur is as likely to steal from her as he is to help her.\
\
'I can afford the risk. I will start small, and if I am cheated, then I will stop trading with them. Would you speak to them on my behalf?'","Upon seeing you return with the crates, Halshûm laughs.\
\
'You did it! If you want to become a Khanda-khêl, let me know. I think you would fit in well.\
\
'I do not want those rations, though. My men have finer tastes than Ordâkhai soldiers do, and I do not expect the dullards to buy them for a third time.'\
\
He chuckles before waving his hand in the air dismissively.\
\
'Do with them what you will. Just get them out of here.'\
\
'Now, on with our business. In Zajâna there is a man named Zarzûmir. You will find him lingering in one of the marketplaces. He would give your jeweller a fair price, and he has caravans that pass through An Shêru, so he could pick up the goods.\
\
'I do business with him myself. He pays me to ensure his caravans make it through An Shêru without being attacked by bandits. Which is very easy to do. I just order them to leave him alone.'\
\
Halshûm laughs again at his own cleverness.\
\
'Anyway, tell Zarzûmir Khanda-mashár sent you, and he will not refuse your offer.'","After helping Halshûm, he gave you the name of a merchant in Zajâna, Zarzûmir, who will do business with Tekâmi. He did not want the Ordâkhai rations that you helped the soldiers of Kôth Rau 'lose' and said you can do whatever you want with them. You should give them to the Jatsakóri in north-eastern An Shêru, as they are always in need of supplies.","'${PLAYER}, you return! But why?'\
\
You present the Ordâkhai rations to the leader of the Jatsakóri and ask Nabatínu if he wants them.\
\
'By the stars, yes! You know we would not turn away any unspoiled food. Thank you for remembering us. You are a treasure.'","Tekâmi has asked you to go to Khanâg Gur and speak with their leader on her behalf about the possibility of a business partnership.","Return to Tekâmi in Jiret-menêsh","Ordâkhai rations 'lost' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the rations to Halshûm at Khanâg Gur","You met with Zarzûmir in Zajâna, and he agreed to trade with Tekâmi. You should return to Jiret-menêsh and tell Tekâmi of your success.","Help the Ordâkhai 'lose' their rations (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the rations to Nabatínu in Gadim-ûn","'Saráz záro-dan, what can Zarzûmir do for you?'\
\
You tell the man that you were sent by Khanda-mashár and that there is a Temámir jeweller in Jiret-menêsh who is looking for a partner to whom she can sell her creations.\
\
'Jewellery? Made by a dwarf in the legendary Jiret-menêsh? Yes, I think I could sell those kinds of goods, no problem, and make a tidy sum at the same time.\
\
'Not that it seems I have a choice, but you do not need to tell me twice to do something that brings in coin. I will assume Khanda-mashár will want a cut, but I will work that out with him. He will also tell me where to find Jiret-menêsh. There are few things he doesn't know. Thank you for bringing me this.'","You went to Khanâg Gur to ask Halshûm if he wanted to do business with Tekâmi. He did not, but he will find someone who does if you do something for him. He wants you to go to Kôth Rau and take back the rations that he recently sold to them, so that they will need to buy more. Kôth Rau is in southern An Shêru.","Tekâmi is worried that she will not be able to find a trade partner, while other dwarves are sending out trade emissaries.","You went to Khanâg Gur to ask Halshûm if he wanted to do business with Tekâmi. He did not, but he will find someone who does if you do something for him. You went to Kôth Rau and took back the ration crates he recently sold to them, so that they will need to buy more. You should return to Halshûm at Khanâg Gur in central An Shêru.","After helping Halshûm, he gave you the name of a merchant in Zajâna, Zarzûmir, who will do business with Tekâmi. You first gave the Ordâkhai rations to the Jatsakóri at Gadim-ûn, and should now go to Zajâna in search of Zarzûmir, who is said to always be in one of the markets."},
[11463]={"Gather crate of swords","'Greetings ${PLAYER}. In the wake of the assault led by Bârshud II we have many people from the area gathering here to volunteer to fight back.\
\
'This warms my heart to see such bravery. I will be busy training the recruits as they are ready but I know that some are still needing to be armed before they can begin. Take some weapons from the crates nearby and arm the recruits with the weapons they desire to learn.'","Recruits armed with swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Some new recruits have volunteered in Iridír after news of the attacks. Bâdarul has asked that you help supply them with weapons so they can begin their training.\
\
Gather supplies of weapons from crates nearby.","Arm the recruits in Iridír with the weapons they desire so that they can begin their training.","Crate of spears gathered","Arm recruits with swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Some new recruits have volunteered in Iridír after news of the attacks. Bâdarul has asked that you help supply them with weapons so they can begin their training.","Arm recruits with bows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gather crate of bows","'The recruits have been arriving and telling me that you supplied them all! I will have them in fighting shape in no time.'","Recruits armed with spears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Crate of bows gathered","Return to Bâdarul","Supplying the Ranks","Gather crate of spears","Arm recruits with spears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Bâdarul in Iridír and inform him that you have armed the new recruits and they are not ready to begin training.","Crate of swords gathered","Recruits armed with bows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11464]={"Lady Góda stands near Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
Ingbert has asked you to speak with his mother, Lady Góda, and learn the heart of her arguments.","Reeve Ingbert, still undecided about what course of action he should take regarding the Orcs in the Entwash Vale, has put his faith in your advice.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You should accept both Support Góda and Support Ingmar to learn their positions, but you may only complete one of them. The other will fail. Which quest you complete will determine who you will support throughout the story arc.</rgb>","If Góda's reasoning seems greater to you than Ingmar's, you should speak with Ingbert on her behalf","Reeve Ingbert stands near Góda in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You should consider Góda's argument. If her reasoning seems preferable to Ingmar's, you should speak with Reeve Ingbert on her behalf.","<rgb=#FF0000>If you complete Support Ingmar, this quest will fail</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Support Góda failed</rgb>","Talk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Talk to Góda in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","You take a moment to convey your support of Góda's position to Reeve Ingbert.\
\
'I understand my son's desire to ride into battle...in my youth, I was much the same. Few beyond Rohan comprehend what it is to earn glory in the heat of battle.\
\
'However, my mother's advice, as you say, seems the greater. My mind is decided: we shall follow Lady Góda's advice.'","'I understand that Tóla sent you to speak with me, to help you convince my son to refuse Ingmar's plan. Indeed, as you have heard, I have been doing just that.\
\
'The argument is moot, for Théoden King's law must rule our decisions. This land is ours only by his command, and we owe our allegiance to him through unbreakable oaths.\
\
'Understand, I do not debate Ingmar's position. If we were permitted, I would be the first to say \\qStrike at the heart of the Enemy!\\q But we ARE restricted. That is why I propose that we strengthen our defences here in Eaworth. Defending a bastion such as this would reduce our losses well beyond what we would see assaulting the Orcs.\
\
'My grandson questions my reasoning, citing the safety of the outlier farms, but many of those farms have already been abandoned, and many more refugees arrive in Eaworth every day. I believe his lust for glory has blinded his sensibilities.\
\
'The greater wisdom says that we should defend Eaworth with all our might. Word has already been sent to Thornhope, our city in the north...I expect further aid from Thane Wulfrad at any moment. Will you defend my position with Ingbert? Consider it well.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You should accept both Support Góda and Support Ingmar to learn their positions, but you may only complete one of them. Which quest you complete will determine who you will support throughout the story arc.</rgb>","'My mother, ${PLAYER}, is a strong woman and wise. She has long been my chief counsellor and has never led me astray. In the matter of the Orcs, she counsels that we refrain from attacking them directly, for Théoden King has forbidden it.\
\
'My loyalty and duty to the King dictates that I comply, yet I am uneasy. Eaworth itself has been raided on numerous occasions, and large numbers of Orcs amass not far from here in clear preparation to lay siege upon us. Why, then, should we refrain from attacking them first, as Ingmar would do?\
\
'Alas, I know not the answer. Speak with my mother and learn the heart of her arguments. Let me know if you decide that hers is the wisest course.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You should accept both Support Góda and Support Ingmar to learn their positions, but you may only complete one of them. The other will fail. Which quest you complete will determine who you will support throughout the story arc.</rgb>","Support Góda"},
[11465]={"<rgb=#FF0000>If you complete Support Góda, this quest will fail</rgb>","Reeve Ingbert, still undecided about what course of action he should take regarding the Orcs in the Entwash Vale, has put his faith in your advice.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You should accept both Support Góda and Support Ingmar to learn their positions, but you may only complete one of them. The other will fail. Which quest you complete will determine who you will support throughout the story arc.</rgb>","Support Ingmar","Lord Ingmar stands near Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
Ingbert has bidden you speak with Ingmar regarding his plan, to learn whether the greater wisdom is to follow his son into battle.","'How I yearn to ride forth with my son against these Orcs who dare intrude upon the lands of the House of Léotharn! Yet I know in my age that my desire, like Ingmar's, is driven more by a lust for glory than for the care of my people.\
\
'I am torn, for I do see reason behind Ingmar's arguments, but is it greater than my mother's? The lives that would be saved by following my mother's advice would be great, but would it resolve the issue of Orcs marauding in the Entwash Vale?\
\
'Speak with Ingmar and learn the full reason behind his plan, then return to me, and I will make my decision.'","Talk to Ingmar in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","You take a moment to convey your support of Ingmar's plan, igniting the passion for glory within Ingbert's heart.\
\
'Aye! I will not remain holed up within these walls like a coward!'\
\
His manner calms a little.\
\
'It is true that we have the opportunity to scatter these Orcs like chaff on the wind... but only if we attack first. I have made my decision.'","Talk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","'Bah! We stand here and debate the wisdom of attacking the Orcs as if driving away invaders in the Entwash Vale could possibly be the motive behind Théoden King's edict.\
\
'There is rumour that Saruman the White, ever the friend and ally of the Rohirrim, has subjected a tribe of Orcs beneath his hand... surely, these are the Orcs which the King protects, yet the invaders are from the Misty Mountains!\
\
'What glory is there in holing up behind these walls, waiting for the Orcs to burn them down around us and kill every man, woman, and child within? It is cowardice!\
\
'Understand, my grandmother is indeed a wise woman, but she is also stubborn. She does not comprehend the opportunity that we have! The Orcs have not yet mustered enough strength to lay siege to Eaworth... if we strike now, we can cripple their efforts and drive the mongrels forth from the Entwash Vale.\
\
'There is no safety within these walls of wood. Fire burns wood, and the Orcs are master wielders of fire. Will you support my position with my father? Perhaps you may bring him courage and wisdom.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You should accept both Support Góda and Support Ingmar to learn their positions, but you may only complete one of them. The other will fail. Which quest you complete will determine who you will support throughout the story arc.</rgb>","If you believe Ingmar's reasoning to be greater than Góda's, you should bring your support of his plan to Ingbert","Ingbert stands near Ingmar in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
If you believe that Ingmar's reasoning is greater than Góda's, you should bring your support of his plan to Ingbert.","<rgb=#FF0000>Support Ingmar failed</rgb>"},
[11466]={"Esta misión te recompensa por tu compra del Paquete de Colaborador de Rivendel Mejorado.","Como ${PLAYERNAME:colaborador[m]|colaboradora[f]}, debes recibir una recompensa por tu contribución. Al aceptar esta misión, recibirás una cantidad de Puntos de LOTRO acorde a tu compra.","Paquete de Colaborador: Rivendel mejorado","Disfruta tu recompensa por ser un colaborador.","Obtén el objeto de adjudicación del paquete de colaborador."},
[11467]={"Paquete de Colaborador: Rivendel Exuberante","Esta misión te recompensa por tu compra del Paquete de Colaborador de Rivendel exuberante.","Como ${PLAYERNAME:colaborador[m]|colaboradora[f]}, debes recibir una recompensa por tu contribución. Al aceptar esta misión, recibirás una cantidad de Puntos de LOTRO acorde a tu compra.","Disfruta tu recompensa por ser un colaborador.","Obtén el objeto de adjudicación del paquete de colaborador."},
[11468]={"Como ${PLAYERNAME:colaborador[m]|colaboradora[f]}, debes recibir una recompensa por tu contribución. Al aceptar esta misión, recibirás una cantidad de Puntos de LOTRO acorde a tu compra.","Paquete de Colaborador: Rivendel simple","Disfruta tu recompensa por ser un colaborador.","Esta misión te recompensa por tu compra del Paquete de Colaborador de Rivendel simple.","Obtén el objeto de adjudicación del paquete de colaborador."},
[11469]={"'Frédéric es sabio. He aprendido mucho observando lo que sucedía en las ruinas. Además, sé que este lugar está repleto de objetos valiosos.\
\
'Si vienes a ayudarnos, ¡te daré la bienvenida!'","'Solo te pido unos instantes de atención, ${PLAYER}, pero ten en cuenta que la tarea que te voy a proponer te llevará más tiempo y te expondrá a peligros reales.\
\
'Hace algún tiempo, antes de que la oscuridad nos invadiera, fuimos testigos de la llegada de los Muertos a Nan Dhelu. Durante mucho tiempo hemos evitado ese lugar, que no nos inspira nada bueno, pero ahora el mal que se encuentra allí aterroriza a nuestro pueblo.\
\
'He enviado allí a una de nuestras mejores guerreras, que está con su compañero, enviado por Stanric. Si quieres ayudarnos, ve a Dol Vaeg para ayudarla. Para llegar allí, sigue el camino hacia el este y busca al norte de la colina más alta.'","Dirígete a las ruinas de Dol Vaeg y habla con Cwendreda. Las ruinas se encuentran al noreste del Gran Camino del Este, en una gran colina.\
\
Fridéric el Anciano te ha pedido que vayas a ver a Cwendreda en Dol Vaeg.","Ve a ver a Cwendreda en Dol Vaeg.","Ayuda a los exploradores","«Sigue el camino hacia el este y busca la colina más alta, al norte. Allí se encuentra Dol Vaeg.'","Fridéric te ha pedido que vayas a ver a Cwendreda, en las ruinas de Dol Vaeg. Esta guerrera se dedica a vigilar a los muertos y a impedir que se extiendan por las ruinas de Nan Dhelu."},
[11470]={"You should talk to the Dumûri captain, Dalagín, on the south side of Iridír, near the river.","Supporting the Bulwark","Talk to Dalagín","'Talk to the captain of the archers on the river-front, Dalagín. See if she requires anything.'","Girhâzi has suggested you assist the Dumûri defending Iridír near the river.","'If you wish to help us hold Iridír, you should head south, to the river-front. There you will find Dumûri archers protecting the city from the Ordâkhai in Eshadûr. Talk to the captain, Dalagín, and see if she requires anything.'","'Girhâzi sent you? It is strange to have an offer of help from an outsider, but I will trust Girhâzi's judgement.'\
\
She sizes you up momentarily as if deciding how much to tell you.\
\
'We are charged with protecting Iridír from a river approach. For a thousand years, there was a grand bridge here called Zibâla, also known as The Flood-span. It was a part of the Road of Riches, and connected Iridír to the fishing village of Eshadûr, on the other side of the Ikorbân.\
\
'It was collapsed one hundred years ago by our people when the Empire of Ordâkh decided our lands should be theirs. Destroying the bridge slowed their advance, but unfortunately failed to keep them out.\
\
'Currently, Ordâkhai forces occupy Eshadûr and it is our duty to make sure that they stay there and do not rebuild the bridge.'"},
[11471]={"El montaraz Culang ha sabido de un gran tesoro enterrado hace mucho tiempo por un terrateniente Dúnadan y quiere recuperarlo antes de que sea encontrado por los saqueadores de tumbas.","El tesoro podría estar bajo otro hito de piedra en algún lugar de Evendim, según el acertijo:\
\
  \\qDesde esta orilla, Rantost puedes divisar,\
  un corto nado es lo que te separa de este lugar.\\q\
\
Debes examinar el hito cuando lo encuentres en busca de alguna pista sobre la localización del tesoro.","'¿Otro acertijo? Te estás burlando de mí, ¿no? ¿Cómo dice este?\
\
 \\qDesde esta orilla, Rantost puedes divisar,\
  un corto nado es lo que te separa de este lugar.\\q\
\
'Rantost es una isla al norte de Tinnudir, reclamada por los saqueadores de tumbas. Busca una playa desde tierra firme desde la que puedas ver Rantost, ¡y apostaría a que podrías encontrar el tesoro!'","Casi en la meta","Encuentra la solución al acertijo","La inscripción en este hito de piedra es apenas legible, pero se pueden distinguir las siguientes palabras:\
\
\
  \\qDesde esta orilla, Rantost puedes divisar,\
  un corto nado es lo que te separa de este lugar.\\q\
\
Este nuevo acertijo podría revelar la verdadera localización del tesoro.","El hito de piedra está rodeado de signos de excavación. Si una vez marcaba la localización del tesoro, seguro que ha sido encontrado.\
\
El hito lleva una inscripción, desgastada por el paso del tiempo.","La inscripción en este hito de piedra es apenas legible, pero se pueden distinguir las siguientes palabras:\
\
  \\qDesde esta orilla, Rantost puedes divisar,\
  un corto nado es lo que te separa de este lugar.\\q\
\
Este nuevo acertijo podría revelar la verdadera localización del tesoro."},
[11472]={"Lleva la bolsita de hierba para pipa a alguien en Rivendel","'¿Un barril de hierba para pipa tirado al lado del camino? Sé que a Pippin le encantaría traer un barril entero si pudiera, pero estoy seguro de que no lo hizo en este viaje.\
\
'Ayer mismo me dijo que sus reservas estaban bajas, y creo que te agradecería esta bolsita, por extrañas que sean las circunstancias.'","Este barril yace a un lado del camino que atraviesa Tâl Bruinen, pero lo más curioso es que está lleno de hierba para pipa. Ya es raro ver carros pasar por aquí, pero carros que transporten hierba para pipa lo son aún más.\
\
Tomas una bolsita de hierba para pipa del barril y decides llevarla a la cercana Rivendel. Quizás alguien allí sepa qué ha provocado que este barril terminara aquí.","'¿Encontraste un barril de hierba para pipa en medio del bosque? Es extraño, pero del tipo de extraño agradable, ¿no crees?\
\
'Yo tengo suficiente, pero Frodo o alguno de sus amigos quizá se haya quedado sin nada y te lo agradecería. Creo que están en mi habitación de la planta baja en este momento.'","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'¿Un barril de hierba para pipa tirado en plena naturaleza? Qué raro. Y por muy bien conservada que esté la hierba, yo no confiaría en ella.'","'¿Encontraste esta hierba para pipa en un barril junto al camino? Qué extraño... y qué suerte: ¡mi bolsita está casi vacía!\
\
'Te lo agradezco, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Pero no te preocupes demasiado por el misterio: fumar hierba para pipa debe estar poniéndose de moda en todos los círculos, no solo entre hobbits y magos. ¿Y por qué no?\
\
'Toma esto con mis agradecimientos.'","Has encontrado un barril lleno de hierba para pipa justo al costado del camino que atraviesa Tâl Bruinen. Algo muy inusual...","Hierba para Pipa Inesperada","Alguien en Rivendel, al norte de Tâl Bruinen, podría saber cómo acabó un barril de hierba para pipa a un lado del camino en medio de la naturaleza.\
\
Has encontrado un barril de hierba para pipa abandonado y has tomado una bolsita para mostrársela a alguien en Rivendel.","'¿Encontraste un barril de hierba para pipa ahí fuera? ¡Tienes buena fortuna, sin duda!\
\
'Pippin casi se ha quedado sin nada y seguro te agradecería esa bolsita que llevas.\
\
'Me pregunto cómo habrá terminado ese barril tirado junto al camino...'"},
[11473]={"Deliver the broken crystal shards to Spall","As you step deeper into Glittengrof, Spall mumbles something to himself","Among the long-abandoned caverns of Gloomingtarn lies Glittengrof, the ancient crystal-lodes of Durin the Deathless.","Glittengrof can be found to the south-west of Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.\
\
Spall has asked you to join him in exploring Glittengrof. You should travel to Glittengrof.","Collected broken crystal shards in Glittengrof (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Spall can be found at your side in Gloomingtarn.\
\
You have collected a number of broken crystal shards in Glittengrof. You should deliver them to Spall.\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.</rgb>","'Will you accompany me to Glittengrof, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'I'm told it is not far from Watchers' Roost, but I have been told a lot of things since I crossed the threshold of Mount Gundabad. And not nearly all of them have proven true! According to legend, it was in Glittengrof that Durin the Deathless first discovered the crystals he would use to light the halls of Mount Gundabad. Perhaps that is why Lord Stormhammer's warriors have not yet returned!\
\
'If Glittengrof is truly so beautiful, I must see it for myself... and not just for my survey! Let us go, my friend!'","Spall can be found at your side in Gloomingtarn.\
\
You have begun your survey of Glittengrof and it appears Spall wishes to speak to you. You should talk to Spall.\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.</rgb>","Surveying Glittengrof","'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'It is a pity that these crystals were damaged, but I will learn what I can from them.'","Broken crystal shards can be found in Glittengrof in Gloomingtarn.\
\
Spall has asked you to collect broken crystal shards from Glittengrof.","Talk to Spall","Explore Glittengrof with Spall","'Alas for Glittengrof!\
\
'If it weren't for these accursed spiders, I could spend hours—nay—days admiring the crystals of Glittengrof! Even their webs have done little to dim their light! I must admit, my friend, I had intended to harvest some of these crystals for my studies, but now I find that I cannot bring myself to raise my pickaxe. To my mind, it would be like defiling an ancient museum!'\
\
Seemingly blind to the danger of the glass-spiders, an awestruck Spall looks around Glittengrof. After a moment, something catches his eye in the distance.\
\
'Wait a moment, ${PLAYER}... do you see that? \
\
'A-ha! It seems that some of the old crystals have fallen to the ground and shattered. If they are just broken shards, I do not feel so badly about collecting them. After all, the spiders have no use for them!\
\
'Will you help me collect some of the shards, my friend?'","Collect broken crystal shards in Glittengrof (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11474]={"Among the long-abandoned caverns of Gloomingtarn lies Ormgren, the ancient ore-lodes of Durin the Deathless.","Surveying Ormgren","Ormgren can be found to the east of Watchers' Roost across Durthuzâram in Gloomingtarn.\
\
Spall has asked you to join him in exploring Ormgren. You should travel to Ormgren.","Spall can be found at your side in Gloomingtarn.\
\
You have begun your survey of Ormgren and it appears Spall wishes to speak to you. You should talk to Spall.\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.</rgb>","'Ah, thank you! These will do nicely, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I hope it was not too much trouble for you, but with these, we might learn what precious minerals still lay hidden within the ancient stones of Mount Gundabad.'","Collected glow-worm gizzards from glow-worms in Ormgren (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Explore Ormgren with Spall","As you step deeper into Ormgren, Spall calls you over","Deliver the glow-worm gizzards to Spall","Glow-worm gizzards can be harvested from adult glow-worms in Ormgren.\
\
Spall has asked you to extract glow-worm gizzards from the glow-worms inhabiting Ormgren.","'By Durin's beard, what has happened to this place?! The glow-worms have been devouring Ormgren from within!'\
\
For a moment, Spall's face drains of colour and it looks as if he is about to faint. After a moment, he steadies himself.\
\
'Perhaps... this was the will of the First Crafter. Yes... yes, it must be. And besides, ${PLAYER}, there is still much to be learned from these glow-worms. It is only a matter of knowing where to look!\
\
'Are you familiar with how glow-worms digest what they eat, my friend? They possess complicated gizzards which become more effective when traces of stones and precious minerals are lodged within them. If we were to collect gizzards from these glow-worms, we might learn what ores and minerals they have recently devoured. And by we, I mean you, of course. I am a proud lore-master, not some butcher of beasts and insects!\
\
'You don't mind helping me, do you? Oh, and only the adult glow-worms will have what I need, so you can leave the wormlets be!'","'Have you heard much of Ormgren, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'From what lore I've been able to gather, it seems that these were among the very first lodes delved in Mount Gundabad—and if legend speaks true, they were first mined by Durin the Deathless himself! I am eager to see how they have fared since the Elder Days, and I hope you are as well, my friend.\
\
'Lord Stormhammer tells me that there is a small boat moored near Skelstrand that we might use to cross Durthuzâram to its eastern banks. I'm not certain how I feel about taking a boat out on the sacred tarn, but even I must admit that swimming seems a poor choice.\
\
'Shall we then?'","Talk to Spall","Spall can be found at your side in Gloomingtarn.\
\
You have collected a number of glow-worm gizzards in Ormgren. You should deliver them to Spall.\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.</rgb>"},
[11475]={"This looks like a good location for the climb","This must be the source of Agarnaith's disease","Complete: Yet Another Bad Plan","'This good spot for climbing. This is gonna work great! I'm the smartest goblin ever! Next stop, Seregost!'","Find a suitable location for Viznak to climb up","Survey the eastern side of Seregost","Viznak has a few ideas for getting into Seregost.\
\
You should complete quests for Viznak.\
\
If Viznak wanders off, you can call him back with the goblin-caller.","'This not gonna be easy. Can't just walk in. But, I got some ideas! Let's try this one!'","Surveying Seregost","Talk to Viznak","Somewhere along Seregost's walls should be a suitable location for the climb.\
\
You should find a suitable location for Viznak to climb up.\
\
If Viznak wanders off, you can call him back with the goblin-caller.","Complete: Another Bad Plan","Your next task is to work with Viznak to discover a way into Seregost. He, of course, has some ideas.","Seregost can be found at the northern end of Agarnaith.\
\
You should survey locations of Seregost's walls.\
\
If Viznak wanders off, you can call him back with the goblin-caller.","'Let's go! I take you to Seregost. No plan yet, we figure it out when we get there. First thing, go look at those walls.\
\
'If you get lost, blow this horn, right? I'll find you.'","Survey the western side of Seregost","Viznak can be called with the goblin-caller.\
\
You should talk to Viznak.","Viznak can be found in his hideout.\
\
You should talk to Viznak when you are ready to go.","There doesn't appear to be an entrance here","Complete: A Bad Plan","Survey central Seregost","'You want into Seregost. This is tough, even with Blight Lady not around. Don't worry, I'll think of something!'"},
[11476]={"Surveying the Morannon","Narchost overlooks much of the western Slag-hills","The entrance does not seem to be heavily guarded","Good vantage points can be found around the Slag-hills.\
\
You should survey the Black Gate and the Towers of the Teeth.","Survey the base of Narchost","'While you are out among the Slag-hills, would you be kind enough to survey the Enemy strongholds of Carchost, Narchost, and the Morannon?\
\
'It is imperative that we have the latest movements of the Enemy.'","You relate to Thurindol what you saw.\
\
'The Morannon has not changed? That is as I expected. The movements you describe around Narchost are interesting. I do not know what to make of it. And Carchost is heavily guarded, you say? That must mean there is something of great importance within the tower now.'","Thurindol requires more information on the structures within the Slag-hills, and wishes for you to survey the territory.","Survey the base of Carchost","You should return to Thurindol, who can be found at the small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.","Survey the tower of Carchost","Return to Thurindol","Travelling any closer to Morannon would surely lead to a swift death","The entrance to the tower seems to be guarded by the entire Orc encampment","Survey the Black Gate","Survey the tower of Narchost","Carchost overlooks much of the eastern Slag-hills"},
[11477]={"Orcos y bandidos derrotados en el Bosque Salvaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Saludos, soy Giles Chadwick. Me alegro de conocerte. Sí, soy miembro de la Hermandad de los Leñadores. Me uní hace poco, cuando me enteré de su gran plan para extraer recursos del Bosque Salvaje y reconstruir el pueblo de Puente de Caballetes. Como puedes ver, el pueblo necesita urgentemente reparaciones tras el ataque de los orcos. He conseguido arreglar algunas cosas pequeñas, aquí y allá, para los habitantes, pero solo soy un leñador.\
\
'Sin embargo, juntos podemos marcar una verdadera diferencia y hacer de Puente de Caballetes el pueblo que debería ser.'","Habla con Nellie Bosquejo","'Fui uno de los primeros defensores de Puente de Caballetes en unirme a la Hermandad de los Leñadores. Aran es un buen hombre, te lo garantizo. ¿Por qué me uní? Bueno, necesitaba seguridad en este pueblo y necesitaba poner orden en mi vida. Los orcos han causado mucho daño y dolor aquí.\
\
'La Hermandad de los Leñadores es el apoyo que yo necesito y que esta ciudad necesita. ¡Les demostraremos a esos orcos que no se puede jugar con Puente de Caballetes!'","El Cruce de Marl, Guardanorte, la Casa del Viejo Risco, el Salón Sobrevino y Guardasur están en el Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías explorar el Bosque Salvaje para la Hermandad de los Leñadores y acabar con cualquier orco o bandido que encuentres.","'¡Veo que hay más fuerzas hostiles en el Bosque Salvaje de lo que pensábamos! La Liga del Hacha será la menor de nuestras preocupaciones mientras nos abrimos paso con cautela por el Bosque Salvaje y recolectamos los abundantes recursos que allí hay. Con tu ayuda, estoy seguro de que venceremos en nuestra causa.'","Habla con Aran Verduno","Las ruinas del Salón Sobrevino ya no están abandonadas","'¿La Hermandad de los Leñadores, eh? ¡Pues sí, soy miembro de la Hermandad! Sería estupendo que te unieras a nosotros. Contar con otra espada para la causa nos ayudará a reconstruir este pueblo más rápido y levantará el ánimo de la buena gente de Puente de Caballetes.\
\
'Sería estupendo que trabajáramos juntos.'","Explora la Casa del Viejo Risco","Habla con Aggy Cavazaña","Guardansur está infestado de enemigos","La Casa del Viejo Risco es un puesto de vigilancia para los enemigos del Bosque Salvaje","'Me alegra saber que deseas unirte a la Hermandad de los Leñadores, ${CLASS}. Tus habilidades serán de gran ayuda para nuestra causa.\
\
'Bien, tu primera misión para la Hermandad consiste en explorar las ruinas y los puntos de interés más destacados del Bosque Salvaje. Creemos que muchas de las antiguas ruinas del Bosque Salvaje pueden haber sido tomadas por orcos o bandidos. Mientras estés en el bosque, derrota a cualquier orco y bandido con el que te encuentres. Es importante que el bosque sea seguro si queremos recolectar sus recursos para la reconstrucción de Puente de Caballetes.'","Explorando las tierras salvajes","Explora el Salón Sobrevino","Guardanorte está infestado de enemigos","Los enemigos de las Quebradas del Norte usan el Cruce de Marl para entrar en el Bosque Salvaje","Explora Guardanorte","Aggy Cavazaña, el guardia Otley, Giles Chadwick y Nellie Bosquejo están en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Deberías hablar con Aggy Cavazaña, el guardia Otley, Giles Chadwick y Nellie Bosquejo cuanto antes.","Explora Guardasur","'Cualquier ${RACE} que goce de buena reputación en Puente de Caballetes es más que bienvenido a unirse a nuestra causa. Si has demostrado tu valía ante quienes viven y residen en este pueblo, entonces ya la has demostrado ante la Hermandad de los Leñadores.\
\
'Sin embargo, no tienes por qué fiarte solo de mi palabra. Si tienes alguna duda sobre unirte a nuestra causa, habla con los habitantes del pueblo. Verás que todo Puente de Caballetes apoya a la Hermandad de los Leñadores y lo que esperamos lograr para el pueblo.'","La Hermandad de los Leñadores desea explorar el Bosque Salvaje de las Tierras de Bree para identificar tanto los recursos como las amenazas que se esconden entre las colinas boscosas.","Habla con Giles Chadwick","Acaba con los orcos y los bandidos en el Bosque Salvaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Explora el Cruce de Marl","Aran Verduno se encuentra en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Deberías hablar con Aran Verduno.","Habla con el guardia Otley","'Sí, por supuesto que conozco la Hermandad de los Leñadores. Fui yo quien les concedió permiso para constituirse y organizarse en Puente de Caballetes. Como sabes, esta ciudad es muy importante para mí. La defendería con mi vida.\
\
'Cualquier ayuda para proteger y reconstruir Puente de Caballetes será más que bienvenida. Te agradecería que colaboraras con la Hermandad para ayudar a mi ciudad.'"},
[11484]={"You have caught Zogmauk's attention.\
\
You should talk to him in Kafagur.","'My injuries? Oh, I'm fine. Getting fixed up right now, aren't I? I'm more worried about Zogmauk, really. Think I scared him -- that's how I landed in this situation.\
\
'He ran away after, but I'm sure he's still somewhere in Kafagur. If you bump into him, make sure he's all right. Just... cough to catch his attention first. He's probably still on edge.'","'Oh. Didn't expect to see you again. Good thing you didn't try to tap me on the shoulder just now -- that was Nargai's mistake.\
\
'It's too quiet here. Nothing like Gundabad. If this were Gundabad, someone would've already cut me down by now. I guess that's why I hid after I hurt Nargai. The only way to survive there was to look out for yourself. But now....\
\
'Take some of this fruit to Nargai, will you? Tell them I said sorry. Maybe I'll be brave enough to say that to their face later.'","Talk to Nargai","Talk to Zogmauk","Nargai has asked you to find and talk to Zogmauk in Kafagur.\
\
They suggested clearing your throat to alert him to your presence first.","'Thanks for checking on Zogmauk. Glad he's doing all right -- or, about as all right as he can be.\
\
'I hope he realizes that he doesn't have to fight anymore. That there's more to living than surviving.'","Find and alert Zogmauk to your presence with a soft <rgb=#00ff00>ahem</rgb>","Survival Instincts","Zogmauk has asked you to return to Nargai with some fruit and his apologies.\
\
Nargai can be found in Kafagur.","Recognition briefly washes over Zogmauk's face as he glances over","Echoes of the violence that the Gundabad Orcs experienced run deeper than mere wounds."},
[11485]={"Collected turtle-hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected turtle-shells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge carne de tortuga (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Survival of the Fittest","Collect turtle-hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${RACE} from afar, will you give us aid? Our food-stores are low and the boats need patching. I have seen great turtles throughout this marsh from which we might obtain sustaining meat, as well as tough hides and shell fragments which we could use to patch the boats and perhaps fashion items to trade.\
\
'Will you help us by hunting the turtles? Bring me meat for our stores, as well as hides and shells, and I will find the means to reward you.\
\
'Thank you for your kindness, ${PLAYER}.'","'These will do wonderfully, ${PLAYER}! Thank you!'","'Have you collected enough turtle-meat, hides, and shells yet?'","Frogildi is at the Woodman camp in the heart of the Rushgore.\
\
You should bring the items you collected to Frogildi.","Has coleccionado carne de tortuga (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Woodmen stranded in the Rushgore are in need of provisions and supplies to see them through their ordeal until they can patch their boats.","Turtles can be found throughout the Rushgore.\
\
Frogildi asked you to hunt the turtles of the Rushgore for their meat, hides, and shells.","Bring the turtle-meat, hides, and shells to Frogildi at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore.","Collect turtle-shells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11486]={"'There are many to look after down here, ${PLAYER}. You have made that task far easier this day.\
\
'You have my thanks.'","Deliver the recovered goods to Echil","Supply-stores can be found hidden throughout Osgiliath.\
\
Echil has asked you to seek out hidden supply-stores and return them to the Rangers of Ithilien within Osgiliath.","Trapped within the tunnels below Osgiliath, the Rangers of Ithilien struggle to survive as their supplies dwindle.","Surviving in the Darkness","'As with weapons and healing herbs, we have hidden numerous supply-stores throughout the city containing rations and fresh water.\
\
'If our stay in this sunken labyrinth is to be a lengthy one, we will have need of those supplies.\
\
'Travel to the surface and search throughout the city for our supply-stores. When you have found as many as you can bear, return them to me!'","Recovered supply-stores in Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Echil can be found in the tunnels beneath Osgiliath.\
\
You have recovered many hidden supply-stores from Osgiliath, and should now deliver them to Echil.","Recover supply-stores in Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11487]={"'You have my thanks, kind ${CLASS}. My strength was fading quickly, and I am not sure how much longer I would have remained conscious. Once I am well enough, I will attempt to make my way to Woodhurst, but it will take time for these wounds to heal.\
\
'In the meantime, I could use your aid in other matters, if you wish to give it.'","'I have been able to further study the map you found. I determined that one of these markings represents an old fortification called Flodgeheld, which lies to the south-west of here along the Swiftwater River. We have not heard from the men who guard it for some time, and they are likely in trouble, have abandoned it, or are dead.\
\
'Please follow the river south-west and find out what state Flodgeheld is in, and if there are any survivors.'","This slain Rohirrim has nothing of use left upon him","'You are not an Orc or Dunlending! I have need of your aid. I was convinced that I would die here. My wounds have grown worse, and I am weak.\
\
'Are you truly there or do my eyes play tricks upon me?'","Talk to Wilberth","You helped wrap the wounds, but Wilberth will need more time to heal","This Rohirrim tried to escape on foot, but was shot down from behind","Flodgeheld lies along the Swiftwater River to the south-west of Brockbridge.\
\
Herefara has asked you to go to Flodgeheld.","You find that Flodgeheld has been attacked recently and should search for survivors","Talk to the injured Rohirrim","This man has wounds from many weapons. He must have fought valiantly to his death","Survivor at Flodgeheld","Find Flodgeheld","Help bandage Wilberth's wounds","One of the two slain Rohirrim you found earlier should have supplies that would aid Wilberth, the injured man you found.","The healing supplies you found will stop Wilberth's health from declining due to the injuries, but it will take some time for him to fully recover.","An injured Rohirrim appears to have hidden himself near the old palisade.\
\
You should speak with the injured Rohirrim and learn what happened at this place.","Flodgeheld lies to the west of Brockbridge.\
\
Flodgeheld appears to have been attacked by the forces of the White Hand. You should scout the area for survivors.","Look for survivors at Flodgeheld (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Wilberth would like to thank you for your aid, as he would probably have died not too long from now without help.","You found a pack with healing supplies","Search slain Rohirrim for healing supplies","Herefara has found that the map contains markings for an old fortification called Flodgeheld. It seems likely to have been attacked by the White Hand as was Brockbridge."},
[11488]={"'I must be off again at once, if I am to find Erkenbrand in time. We must reach the Hornburg before the Uruks are done with it, on foot but for Shadowfax, if Elfhelm's reports are to be believed.\
\
'Fare well to you, ${PLAYER}! I hope you will join me in my search for the lords of the Westfold, when you are able!'","Bring the news of Grimbold to Hildith","Elfhelm is in his camp in the passage through the mountains in the southern Westfold.\
\
You should speak with Elfhelm before he departs for Meduseld.","Speak with Elfhelm","Gandalf is at Elfhelm's Camp in the passage through the mountains in the southern Westfold.\
\
You should speak with Gandalf.","Hildith is pale as you relay Elfhelm's harsh account of Grimbold's failed decisions at the Fords of Isen.\
\
'He wanted to stay because he had nothing to lose. I cursed my husband when he left, he who has always been kind to me.\
\
'My poor husband must be suffering much, if he is still alive. First I withdrew my support, and then Elfhelm followed in the heat of battle. He will be shattered....'","Observe the end of the Second Battle of the Fords","Hildith is in the Mead Hall of Grimslade.\
\
You should return to Hildith with the news of her husband.","'Well met, ${PLAYER}! I have found the lord Elfhelm...and so have you, for that matter.\
\
'I have had news of Erkenbrand and Grimbold at last, after much searching. I believe they will be far to the west from here, nearer to Helm's Deep than I dared hope. Elfhelm and Grimbold did not part as friends.\
\
'Elfhelm is about to depart for Edoras to protect the king's own city. If you have anything to ask of him, you should do so now, before he departs.'","Habla con Gandalf","You have found Elfhelm, one of the missing lords from the Fords of Isen. He will have word of the other lords who went missing when the fords fell to the enemy.","Survivors From the Fords","Elfhelm is willing to tell you of the last time he saw Grimbold","'It grieves me to hear that Lady Hildith begs word of Grimbold, for I have nothing much to give. I will tell you all that I can of our parting, and you may feel free to relay the message to the lady.'"},
[11489]={"The third suspicious character, possibly a Corsair in disguise, can be found somewhere around the warehouses of Dol Amroth.\
\
You should investigate the third suspicious character.","'Captain Abedec sends his regards, ${PLAYER}. It seems we have found you at last.\
\
'Now, where is Jajax? The Captain wants his head atop the mast of his ship to answer for his crimes. It will look nice next to yours!'","Lothíriel has heard reports of Corsair scouts who may have infiltrated the great city of Dol Amroth.","Investigate the suspicious person in the Court of the Fount","Speak with the swan-knight guard outside the door","'Ho there! I've been looking for you, ${PLAYER}, but the people of this city only give me strange looks, and never answers.'\
\
You cannot help but laugh at Jajax's brazen appearance in the city of his enemies.\
\
'Why do you laugh? I left much of my armour behind, and wrapped myself in this flimsy lady's cloak, like the men here do. Is the disguise insufficient?\
\
'In all seriousness, my friend, I am glad to see you. You have defeated all but one of the Captains of the Corsairs. Only Abedec remains, and he is the deadliest and cruelest of all....'","The second suspicious character, possibly a Corsair in disguise, can be found somewhere around the wharf of Dol Amroth.\
\
You should investigate the second suspicious character.","You have defeated the disguised Corsair in the Court of the Fount, but his threats were unsettling...","Suspicious Characters in Dol Amroth","'So you're the one Captain Abedec is looking for! I've been searching for you, ${PLAYER}... you and your friend Captain Jajax.\
\
'You and Jajax are both dead! I'll tell Abedec you're here, and you'll rue the day you crossed the Corsairs.'","The swan-knight guard can be found outside of the Great Hall of the Prince.\
\
You should ask the swan-knight guard where suspicious folk are being investigated.","'I have heard troubling reports, ${PLAYER}, and the swan-knights are doing everything in their power to confirm or deny them. Some suspicious folk have been seen in the city, which in itself is not alarming, but I have reason to believe that the Corsairs are attempting to scout Dol Amroth.\
\
'These are good people here, and they are not warriors. An attack on Dol Amroth by the Corsairs could be devastating.\
\
'Speak with the guards, if you wish to help. They are investigating the latest reports.'","Evidently the suspicious characters have been searching for you...","The first suspicious character, possibly a Corsair in disguise, can be found somewhere around the Court of the Fount.\
\
You should investigate the first suspicious character.","Captain Abedec's threats are severe indeed, but empty thus far","Investigate the suspicious person at the wharf","'The Lady Lothíriel sent you to look into the rumours of suspicious folk? I will tell you all that I have heard.\
\
'One report was in the Court of the Fount, another on the wharf, and the last around the warehouses. Come to think of it, all of them were asking around about a person meeting your description....'","Investigate the suspicious person at the warehouses"},
[11490]={"Quienquiera que haya levantado este campamento puede haber dejado algo atrás.\
\
Deberías registrar el campamento en busca de información.","Examina la hoguera","Examina las huellas","Habla con Lagordal","'¿Un dunlendino te tendió una emboscada? Entonces hacía bien en desconfiar, pues son gente odiosa que no se detendrá ante nada para estorbarnos.\
\
'Ya estamos bastante desbordados de por sí... ¡lo último que necesitábamos era que Saruman dirigiera su mirada hacia el Ángulo!'","Has encontrado un par de rastros de vida en este campamento.\
\
Deberías examinar las huellas para obtener más información.","Puede que esté teniendo lugar alguna actividad funesta bajo las narices de los Montaraces.","Un saco a medio llenar con provisiones podridas yace flácido en el suelo","En el momento en que intentaste examinar las huellas del campamento, un dunlendino te atacó.\
\
Deberías volver a Lagordal con estas noticias.","Lagordal te ha pedido que investigues un campamento sospechoso en lo alto de un acantilado.\
\
El acantilado se encuentra al sureste, junto a la cascada que hay frente a Tornhad.","La tierra cubre parte de esta hoguera, como si alguien hubiera intentado enterrarla a toda prisa","'No te preocupes por mí... es una herida leve, nada más. Uno de mis compañeros Montaraces está buscando a un sanador en este mismo instante.\
\
'¿Ves ese acantilado al sureste, junto a la cascada? Allí encontré un campamento extraño, sin un alma a la vista. Pero lo dejé estar, con la intención de completar primero una tarea que me habían asignado. Como ves, no he podido volver para investigar.\
\
'Sospecho que una gente... bastante indeseable se ha abierto camino hacia el norte hasta esta región. Con qué propósito, lo desconozco.\
\
'¿Te encargarías tú de investigar el campamento? Cuéntame lo que averigües.'","Encuentra el campamento sospechoso","Rastros sospechosos en el Ángulo","Examina el saco","¡Una ramita se parte detrás de ti!","El campamento ha sido abandonado"},
[11491]={"Los Angmarim recorren Eregion en busca de cualquier vestigio del pasado que pueda reforzar aún más sus fuerzas. El pequeño grupo de elfos que se encuentra en Echad Mirobel desea conservar las ruinas tal y como están, y te ha pedido que les ayudes en esta misión.","Sospechoso por naturaleza","'¿Ya has encontrado a un herrero? Me temo que se nos acaba el tiempo.'","Consigue la Marca de Angmar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Marca de Angmar conseguida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Junto con las noticias que nos llegan de los exploradores de todo Eregion y de las zonas más cercanas, la confirmación de la existencia de este herrero es una grave noticia. Aun así, me reconforta saber que ha muerto y que ya no podrá ayudar al enemigo.'","En Mirobel, en la región suroeste de Eregion, hay un herrero.\
\
Ornras de Echad Mirobel te ha pedido que derrotes a los enemigos de esa región y, con suerte, encuentres a alguien que lleve la Marca de Angmar. La presencia de un gran herrero oculto entre los enemigos de menor rango explicaría por qué algunos de los líderes de este ejército del norte llevan consigo un mineral poderoso y maligno.","'Odio tener que hacer esto, pero debo pedirte que disipes mis temores y regreses a Mirobel, junto a los Angmarim que allí se encuentran. Ya has hecho mucho, pero las penurias nunca terminan cuando se tiene a estos enemigos cerca.\
\
'Mi corazón me advierte de que entre los Angmarim hay un herrero capaz de trabajar con el hierro que has descubierto. Te pediría que regresaras a Mirobel y registraras a muchos Angmarim allí. Es muy posible que encuentres a un herrero que lleve una Marca de Angmar. De hecho, espero que así sea.\
\
'He visto estas marcas antes y denotan un nivel de respeto hacia la destreza del herrero que posee el objeto. Solo un gran herrero llevaría una, y solo un gran herrero trabajaría con el mineral maligno que has encontrado. Si eliminas a este herrero, el portador de la Marca, podrías contribuir más de lo que imaginas a obstaculizar la sombría labor de esta presencia procedente del norte.'","Devuelve la Marca a Ornras en Echad Mirobel"},
[11496]={"Las barricadas que se encuentren en Guardasur deben destruirse para debilitar las defensas de tus enemigos en el Bosque Salvaje.","Destruye barricadas en Guardasur","En Guardasur, en el Bosque Salvaje, hay barricadas.\
\
Debes destruir las barricadas de Guardasur.","Los enemigos de los Pueblos Libres han fortificado la torre de Guardasur en el Bosque Salvaje. Si destruimos las barricadas de este lugar, debilitaremos las defensas de Guardasur.","Guardasur: Destrucción de barricadas","Destruye barricadas en Guardasur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Barricadas destruidas en Guardasur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11497]={"Acaba con enemigos en Guardasur","Es necesario derrotar a los enemigos de los Pueblos Libres que se encuentran en Guardasur para proteger a los habitantes del Bosque Salvaje.","Acaba con enemigos en Guardasur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Guardasur: Enemigos de los Pueblos Libres","En Guardasur, en el Bosque Salvaje, hay enemigos.\
\
Debes derrotar a los enemigos en Guardasur.","Enemigos derrotados en Guardasur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los enemigos de los Pueblos Libres se han apoderado de la torre de Guardasur, en el Bosque Salvaje. Derrotarlos aquí contribuirá a devolver la paz al Bosque Salvaje."},
[11498]={"'Eres más fuerte de lo que pareces para cazar tan bien en Malenhad.'","'¿El Antiguo Escamahierro es un desafío demasiado grande para ti, ${PLAYERNAME:sureño[m]|sureña[f]}? No me sorprende.'","'¿Qué? ¿Has matado al Antiguo Escamahierro? ¡Estoy asombrado! No esperaba que siquiera lo intentaras, después de contarte lo terrible que es.\
\
'Debo ser honesto contigo, ${PLAYERNAME:sureño[m]|sureña[f]}, no era exactamente el enemigo legendario que te presenté. De hecho, nosotros los cazadores buscamos a esta bestia cuando llegamos a la mayoría de edad en un antiguo ritual entre nuestro pueblo. Por supuesto, no todos los jóvenes regresan de estas cacerías...\
\
'Pero aún así, es un gran logro para alguien que no nació en las duras colinas y los pantanos fétidos del Norte. Debo felicitarte por esta hazaña digna de elogio. Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un verdadero cazador[m]|una verdadera cazadora[f]} de Angmar.'","Othran se encuentra en su campamento, en la parte occidental de Malenhad.\
\
Deberías volver a Othran para contarle la historia de tu victoria contra el temido Antiguo Escamahierro.","El raro Antiguo Escamahierro se puede encontrar a veces entre sus hermanos menores en el pantano de Malenhad.\
\
Othran te ha desafiado a ti y a tus compañeros a matar al temido Antiguo Escamahierro, señor de las tortugas maléficas de Malenhad.","Habitante del pantano","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido, poderoso[m]|Bienvenida, poderosa[f]} , ${PLAYERNAME:asesino[m]|asesina[f]} del temido Escamahierro.'","'Entonces, ${PLAYERNAME:sureño[m]|sureña[f]}, has demostrado ser más que ${PLAYERNAME:digno[m]|digna[f]} de cazar en el pantano de azufre de Malenhad. ¿Quizás quieras ganar aún más gloria? Hay presas en este pantano que son demasiado peligrosas incluso para nosotros, que hemos cazado estos pantanos desde tiempos inmemoriales.\
\
'Hablo del temido Antiguo Escamahierro, un monstruo tan mortal que ninguno de mi pueblo lo ha enfrentado... y sobrevivió para contar la historia.\
\
'Creo que será imposible para alguien en solitario, por valiente que sea, derrotar a tal enemigo, pero incluso si pudieras, con compañeros, matar a esta bestia, me vería obligado a admitir que eres verdaderos cazadores y guerreros de renombre. El Antiguo Escamahierro es una bestia rara, pero a veces se puede encontrar entre sus hermanos menores en el pantano.'","El pantano de azufre de Malenhad también alberga una terrible bestia, que los montañeses llaman el \\qAntiguo Escamahierro\\q."},
[11499]={"Se busca: ramas sin punta de los terribles trolls silvanos y otros árboles particularmente enfadados en la Ciénaga de los Cisnes. ¡Se ofrece una recompensa adecuada en el momento de la entrega!","Recoger ramas sin punta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tarea de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes: Ramas sin punta","Entregar las ramas sin punta en un buzón de recogida","Has entregado un lote de trofeos a cambio de una modesta recompensa adecuada para un coleccionista como tú.","Ramas sin punta recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has aceptado una tarea para adquirir ramas sin punta.","Un habitante de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes ha publicado una tarea para recoger ramas sin punta."},
}
